1
00:02:12,003 --> 00:02:14,003
[pleasant music playing]

2
00:02:34,522 --> 00:02:35,928
[traffic bustling sounds]

3
00:02:39,610 --> 00:02:40,341
Are you done?

4
00:02:40,984 --> 00:02:42,478
How do I look?

5
00:02:42,965 --> 00:02:46,215
Like a proper, traditional
daughter of the house.

6
00:02:46,509 --> 00:02:48,482
Traditional what?

7
00:02:48,506 --> 00:02:50,173
A traditional woman.

8
00:02:54,810 --> 00:02:56,658
[pleasant music continues]

9
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:09,113
Are you nervous?

10
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,896
Are you?

11
00:03:12,674 --> 00:03:15,174
Well, it's been almost 3 years.

12
00:03:15,757 --> 00:03:18,007
I wonder how they will receive us.

13
00:03:18,585 --> 00:03:21,752
Trust me. All their anger will
disappear the moment they see you.

14
00:03:23,257 --> 00:03:26,841
I'm sure they will fall
in love with you too.

15
00:03:26,971 --> 00:03:28,276
They have no choice.

16
00:03:28,301 --> 00:03:30,468
I'll keep trying till they do.

17
00:03:30,702 --> 00:03:31,715
Just wait and watch.

18
00:03:32,011 --> 00:03:33,195
I got a whole plan laid out.

19
00:03:33,381 --> 00:03:35,637
Well, don't get your hopes up.

20
00:03:35,662 --> 00:03:36,583
Oh, they're already up.

21
00:03:36,657 --> 00:03:38,530
I want everyone to like me.

22
00:03:38,895 --> 00:03:40,257
Oh...

23
00:03:40,945 --> 00:03:41,945
Is that so?

24
00:03:47,168 --> 00:03:48,181
[sighs]

25
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:52,948
Actually, I'm scared they
might say something to you.

26
00:03:55,926 --> 00:03:59,367
I mean, you did snatch me
away from my family, after all.

27
00:04:01,817 --> 00:04:02,817
Not my words.

28
00:04:02,842 --> 00:04:04,425
It's what my family would say.

29
00:04:06,818 --> 00:04:07,777
Swarna...

30
00:04:08,543 --> 00:04:11,001
You know I was kidding, right?

31
00:04:12,732 --> 00:04:13,648
Come on.

32
00:04:16,743 --> 00:04:19,148
Grandpa, my husband is a good doctor.

33
00:04:19,231 --> 00:04:22,356
Feel free to get checked.
It's free of cost.

34
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:23,898
Doctor, my leg hurts all the time.

35
00:04:23,923 --> 00:04:27,502
Please take a look at this.

36
00:04:27,527 --> 00:04:29,527
[overlapping voices]

37
00:04:31,024 --> 00:04:32,277
Everyone will get their turn.

38
00:04:32,302 --> 00:04:34,561
Okay, okay. Calm down.

39
00:04:34,586 --> 00:04:36,095
[laughs]

40
00:04:45,315 --> 00:04:47,356
Stop the bus!

41
00:04:47,387 --> 00:04:49,070
-Veerendar Raju!
-Long Live!

42
00:04:49,095 --> 00:04:50,757
-Veerendar Raju!
-Long Live!

43
00:04:50,782 --> 00:04:53,824
Get down, everyone. The bus
won't go beyond this point.

44
00:04:55,058 --> 00:04:59,273
-Veerendar Raju!
-Long Live!

45
00:05:03,666 --> 00:05:05,385
[traffic bustling sounds]

46
00:05:09,106 --> 00:05:10,095
Sit here.

47
00:05:11,273 --> 00:05:13,982
Swarna, I'll go find something to eat.

48
00:05:17,572 --> 00:05:19,114
Hey, get me a cup of tea.

49
00:05:20,697 --> 00:05:21,795
Block the other side too.

50
00:05:25,912 --> 00:05:29,267
I'm sure you worked very
hard to gather all these people,

51
00:05:29,297 --> 00:05:30,842
and move these stones here.

52
00:05:30,867 --> 00:05:33,742
Of course! We had to wake up at 4 AM.

53
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:37,069
Please don't mind me asking.

54
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:40,790
Will his soul rest in peace if
you shut everything down?

55
00:05:40,815 --> 00:05:41,996
What's the logic here?

56
00:05:42,727 --> 00:05:46,671
Not just the roads. Schools,
shops, everything is shut down.

57
00:05:46,696 --> 00:05:49,655
It's a way of paying
respect to his soul.

58
00:05:50,923 --> 00:05:53,797
Respect or peace for his soul?
They are two different things.

59
00:05:53,826 --> 00:05:54,939
Check the other side, guys.

60
00:05:55,399 --> 00:05:57,417
His soul will rest in
peace if we respect him.

61
00:06:00,725 --> 00:06:01,765
[smirks]

62
00:06:02,948 --> 00:06:04,238
Take a tea break, guys.

63
00:06:07,145 --> 00:06:11,031
But until yesterday, people
were using the roads as usual.

64
00:06:11,055 --> 00:06:12,714
All the shops were operating.

65
00:06:12,739 --> 00:06:14,905
Does that mean they were
disrespecting him then?

66
00:06:15,773 --> 00:06:18,572
When he was with us, we were
respecting him directly in person.

67
00:06:18,597 --> 00:06:21,848
Now that he's gone, what's
wrong in showing it like this?

68
00:06:23,168 --> 00:06:25,168
Where did you get these flags?

69
00:06:25,935 --> 00:06:27,810
Rangaiah's tailoring shop.

70
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:31,096
Oh! So you opened the shops
even after he passed away.

71
00:06:31,375 --> 00:06:33,159
Just for half an hour.
And then we shut it again.

72
00:06:33,183 --> 00:06:34,866
What about the tea and coffee?

73
00:06:35,058 --> 00:06:37,325
Savithramma's
tea shop. So what?

74
00:06:37,349 --> 00:06:38,410
What are you implying?

75
00:06:38,435 --> 00:06:41,962
Half an hour for the flags
and 15 minutes for the tea.

76
00:06:41,987 --> 00:06:44,074
Another 30 minutes for the garlands.

77
00:06:44,098 --> 00:06:47,754
Looks like you've disrespected
him more than any of us.

78
00:06:47,779 --> 00:06:49,462
Are you saying we
disrespected our leader?

79
00:06:49,487 --> 00:06:50,749
Hold on a minute!

80
00:06:50,774 --> 00:06:53,538
What did you just say?
We're disrespecting our leader?

81
00:06:53,563 --> 00:06:54,489
Where are you from, again?

82
00:06:54,544 --> 00:06:57,175
[overlapping clamor]

83
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,819
Swarna, what's going on?

84
00:07:05,844 --> 00:07:08,719
Calm down, guys. Let's talk.

85
00:07:08,744 --> 00:07:10,367
Please calm down.

86
00:07:10,392 --> 00:07:11,600
Stop pushing me!

87
00:07:11,615 --> 00:07:12,590
[hand swishing]

88
00:07:12,614 --> 00:07:13,739
Suri!

89
00:07:13,797 --> 00:07:15,838
Did he just fall in?

90
00:07:15,988 --> 00:07:17,485
Is he alive?

91
00:07:17,547 --> 00:07:18,964
My husband is a good doctor.

92
00:07:19,652 --> 00:07:21,591
[playful music playing]

93
00:07:27,178 --> 00:07:29,065
[traffic bustling sounds]

94
00:07:37,018 --> 00:07:38,930
[bus comes to a halt]

95
00:07:49,868 --> 00:07:52,040
My brother said he'd pick us up.

96
00:07:52,065 --> 00:07:53,927
It's okay. The bus was late, right?

97
00:07:54,834 --> 00:07:56,167
Taxi, taxi!

98
00:07:57,778 --> 00:07:58,773
Taxi!

99
00:07:58,870 --> 00:07:59,711
Swarna, let's go.

100
00:08:00,513 --> 00:08:02,300
[eerie music playing]

101
00:08:10,556 --> 00:08:11,411
Let me get that.

102
00:08:34,892 --> 00:08:36,392
Brother, how are you?

103
00:08:36,417 --> 00:08:37,458
Hey, take this inside.

104
00:08:39,017 --> 00:08:40,101
Sister-in-law, how are you?

105
00:08:41,392 --> 00:08:42,461
Let me take these.

106
00:08:43,059 --> 00:08:43,976
Here you go.

107
00:08:44,499 --> 00:08:46,362
I waited at the bus stop for so long.

108
00:08:46,387 --> 00:08:47,914
But then I had to rush back here.

109
00:08:47,944 --> 00:08:50,312
Our bus was interrupted
by a group of protestors.

110
00:08:51,065 --> 00:08:53,273
Umm... Geetha has been asking for you.

111
00:08:54,235 --> 00:08:56,069
And for sister-in-law, of course.

112
00:08:56,167 --> 00:08:57,001
Please come.

113
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:00,705
-Listen, I need to tell you something.
-What is it?

114
00:09:01,213 --> 00:09:02,737
Dad doesn't know you're coming.

115
00:09:05,136 --> 00:09:07,511
Are you serious? You said you told him.

116
00:09:07,552 --> 00:09:09,842
I didn't say that.

117
00:09:09,867 --> 00:09:11,271
I said I was going to tell him.

118
00:09:12,045 --> 00:09:13,397
Why didn't you tell him then?

119
00:09:13,518 --> 00:09:14,885
I'll find the right time and tell him.

120
00:09:14,917 --> 00:09:17,108
You come inside. Sister-in-law, let's go.

121
00:09:18,136 --> 00:09:18,954
Swarna...

122
00:09:18,979 --> 00:09:20,354
Priest, the auspicious
time will pass. Let's go.

123
00:09:20,411 --> 00:09:21,120
Sure, sir.

124
00:09:21,469 --> 00:09:24,641
[priest chanting]

125
00:09:25,596 --> 00:09:27,220
I'll read out the wedding invitation now.

126
00:09:27,403 --> 00:09:29,880
Wishing the couple a
blessed and harmonious life,

127
00:09:30,386 --> 00:09:31,928
On the first day of
the bright fortnight...

128
00:09:32,452 --> 00:09:34,380
Mom, look! Big brother's here!

129
00:09:34,405 --> 00:09:36,053
of the month of Jyeshta, in the
lunar year named Krodhanama,

130
00:09:36,078 --> 00:09:39,933
this auspicious time has
been set for the wedding of...

131
00:09:39,957 --> 00:09:42,803
Ramaiah Raju’s second
daughter Venkata Geetha with...

132
00:09:42,886 --> 00:09:50,219
and Uppalapati Madhava
Raju's only son Prakash...

133
00:09:50,251 --> 00:09:53,292
in holy matrimony, with
the blessings of Almighty.

134
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,342
Sir, please exchange
the ceremonial offerings.

135
00:09:56,630 --> 00:09:59,750
[priest continues chanting]

136
00:10:16,688 --> 00:10:17,995
Hello, sister-in-law.

137
00:10:21,993 --> 00:10:23,033
[smiles]

138
00:10:27,865 --> 00:10:29,858
[suspenseful music playing]

139
00:10:31,891 --> 00:10:34,164
Now watch your dad go off at him!

140
00:10:34,765 --> 00:10:36,181
Who called him?

141
00:10:36,770 --> 00:10:38,312
Actually...

142
00:10:38,782 --> 00:10:41,157
I did. I was going to tell you...

143
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,994
You thought I wouldn't be able
to say anything once he's here.

144
00:10:44,926 --> 00:10:48,218
He left this family for that woman.

145
00:10:48,485 --> 00:10:51,152
How could he even show up now?

146
00:10:51,886 --> 00:10:55,489
But our sister deserves to have
her elder brother at her wedding.

147
00:10:57,208 --> 00:10:58,875
-I'll see you.
-Yeah.

148
00:10:59,341 --> 00:11:00,334
Let's go.

149
00:11:08,816 --> 00:11:10,816
We're at a wedding
where we aren't welcome.

150
00:11:11,746 --> 00:11:13,412
They refuse to even talk to me.

151
00:11:13,941 --> 00:11:14,935
It's okay.

152
00:11:15,927 --> 00:11:17,693
Nobody greeted me either.

153
00:11:19,294 --> 00:11:22,023
Anyway, the function is over.

154
00:11:22,736 --> 00:11:23,569
Let's go.

155
00:11:24,251 --> 00:11:25,626
Brother, hello!

156
00:11:25,651 --> 00:11:27,835
Where do you think you're going?

157
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:31,110
You didn't wish me well or shake
my hand. What is this behavior?

158
00:11:31,196 --> 00:11:32,530
All the best!

159
00:11:32,766 --> 00:11:34,122
The guy looks really good.

160
00:11:34,209 --> 00:11:35,168
I know, right.

161
00:11:35,293 --> 00:11:36,937
Alright then. We'll leave.

162
00:11:37,103 --> 00:11:39,144
Hello, sir! Won't you
stay for the wedding?

163
00:11:39,589 --> 00:11:42,214
I can't manage everything alone.
You have to stay.

164
00:11:43,139 --> 00:11:44,389
You know how dad can be.

165
00:11:44,618 --> 00:11:45,992
Please stay.

166
00:11:46,249 --> 00:11:47,541
Sister-in-law, please.

167
00:11:47,805 --> 00:11:49,014
Let's stay, Ani.

168
00:11:49,632 --> 00:11:51,674
Oh! You call him Ani.

169
00:11:54,806 --> 00:11:57,473
We came all the way.
We might as well stay.

170
00:11:57,838 --> 00:11:59,546
They seem like such good people.

171
00:11:59,964 --> 00:12:00,731
Mom...

172
00:12:01,062 --> 00:12:04,109
Are you taking out your resentment
toward your father on us?

173
00:12:04,342 --> 00:12:05,754
Won't you stay back
for your mother’s sake?

174
00:12:08,367 --> 00:12:09,416
Just wait and see.

175
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:11,973
We'll become their
favorites within a week.

176
00:12:15,313 --> 00:12:16,788
[sifting rice]

177
00:12:16,827 --> 00:12:18,622
[waving hand fan]

178
00:12:20,674 --> 00:12:21,823
Don't be so sure.

179
00:12:21,911 --> 00:12:24,936
The enquiry commission is yet to begin.

180
00:12:26,269 --> 00:12:27,436
What are you?

181
00:12:28,817 --> 00:12:29,900
What?

182
00:12:30,779 --> 00:12:31,654
I'm Swarna.

183
00:12:33,447 --> 00:12:34,724
That's what you
wanted to know, right?

184
00:12:35,007 --> 00:12:37,701
She's asking about your caste.

185
00:12:37,728 --> 00:12:39,634
Oh, sorry.

186
00:12:40,349 --> 00:12:42,359
Unfortunately, my parents passed away...

187
00:12:42,383 --> 00:12:44,890
before I could know my caste.

188
00:12:46,142 --> 00:12:48,809
I'd have definitely asked
them if they lived a little longer.

189
00:12:48,834 --> 00:12:53,417
That's sad. What about
properties, assets, gold, etc?

190
00:12:53,713 --> 00:12:56,573
Unfortunately, I missed out on that too.

191
00:12:56,894 --> 00:12:59,856
-Did you go to college?
-I did BA Economics.

192
00:12:59,894 --> 00:13:01,520
What's that all about?

193
00:13:02,878 --> 00:13:04,882
Well, Economics is...

194
00:13:05,044 --> 00:13:06,689
It's nothing, grandma.

195
00:13:06,713 --> 00:13:09,395
Few degrees are purely
decorative, and this is one of them.

196
00:13:09,875 --> 00:13:11,000
Let me answer.

197
00:13:13,334 --> 00:13:14,244
Economics is...

198
00:13:14,268 --> 00:13:16,101
Which side are you from anyway?

199
00:13:16,798 --> 00:13:17,714
Side.

200
00:13:19,396 --> 00:13:20,762
It's not caste. So...

201
00:13:21,439 --> 00:13:24,253
She means to ask where you're from.

202
00:13:24,327 --> 00:13:25,799
Your slang is a bit eccentric.

203
00:13:25,824 --> 00:13:27,395
So she wants to know your native place.

204
00:13:27,419 --> 00:13:31,086
We stayed in Tirupati for
a while, and then Nellore.

205
00:13:31,163 --> 00:13:33,278
They're adjacent regions.

206
00:13:33,437 --> 00:13:35,437
What about coo...coo...coo...

207
00:13:35,514 --> 00:13:36,639
Let me say it.

208
00:13:37,945 --> 00:13:39,444
She's asking if you can cook.

209
00:13:39,807 --> 00:13:41,013
[chuckles awkwardly]

210
00:13:41,352 --> 00:13:43,079
When do you wake up in the morning?

211
00:13:43,103 --> 00:13:44,811
Can you make Methi Muttton Masala?

212
00:13:44,905 --> 00:13:46,218
What was your percentage in BA?

213
00:13:46,243 --> 00:13:47,718
Can you do Surya Namaskars?

214
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:49,343
What about tamarind chicken?

215
00:13:49,368 --> 00:13:50,509
Can you sew?

216
00:13:50,534 --> 00:13:51,673
Can you make rangolis?

217
00:13:51,697 --> 00:13:52,714
Do you have any siblings?

218
00:13:53,784 --> 00:13:56,175
They grilled me like I'm some criminal.

219
00:13:56,477 --> 00:13:58,236
I wonder where he found her.

220
00:13:58,261 --> 00:14:00,565
What's wrong with my accent?

221
00:14:00,655 --> 00:14:02,212
I speak just like you, right?

222
00:14:02,236 --> 00:14:03,936
What was up with that accent?

223
00:14:04,108 --> 00:14:07,189
Oh, god! Was it Tamil or Telugu?

224
00:14:07,351 --> 00:14:09,268
How did you put up with them, Ani?

225
00:14:09,293 --> 00:14:10,960
How is he putting up with her?

226
00:14:11,310 --> 00:14:13,435
Do you think she will mingle with us?

227
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:18,059
Tamarind Chicken.

228
00:14:18,442 --> 00:14:20,651
Methi Mutton Masala.

229
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:23,686
Just wait. I will hit them so hard!

230
00:14:25,713 --> 00:14:27,161
With love, Ani.

231
00:14:31,103 --> 00:14:32,669
-All hail...
-Mr. Ramaiah Raju!

232
00:14:32,694 --> 00:14:34,191
-All hail...
-Mr. Ramaiah Raju!

233
00:14:34,232 --> 00:14:36,158
[bustling slogans]

234
00:14:40,776 --> 00:14:43,591
-Namaste, sir.
-Namaste.

235
00:14:44,110 --> 00:14:44,857
Please come.

236
00:14:45,199 --> 00:14:46,536
How did the engagement go?

237
00:14:46,561 --> 00:14:47,954
We heard your elder son
and daughter-in-law are here.

238
00:14:47,978 --> 00:14:49,768
Did you send the candidate
list to the party's Head Office?

239
00:14:49,793 --> 00:14:51,881
-We wanted to check with you first.
-Get on it right away.

240
00:14:52,990 --> 00:14:57,115
-Namaste, sir.
-Namaste.

241
00:14:57,995 --> 00:14:59,921
[unsettling music playing]

242
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:07,448
Please be seated.

243
00:15:12,424 --> 00:15:15,140
Greetings to the candidates
and members of our party.

244
00:15:15,165 --> 00:15:16,366
Namaste, sir.

245
00:15:16,739 --> 00:15:20,111
There have been discussions
with the High Command...

246
00:15:20,136 --> 00:15:21,928
about who should get
the party ticket next.

247
00:15:21,966 --> 00:15:25,164
Only a candidate with
a good public image,

248
00:15:25,189 --> 00:15:27,725
-Hail!
-Madhusudhan Rao.

249
00:15:29,992 --> 00:15:31,367
someone experienced,

250
00:15:31,392 --> 00:15:33,893
-Hail!
-Madhusudhan Rao.

251
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:36,117
someone deserving,

252
00:15:36,142 --> 00:15:38,582
-Hail!
-Madhusudhan Rao.

253
00:15:38,668 --> 00:15:40,566
someone away from
scams and criminal cases,

254
00:15:40,591 --> 00:15:42,428
-Hail!
-Madhusudhan Rao!

255
00:15:42,453 --> 00:15:43,655
Stop it!

256
00:15:46,731 --> 00:15:50,606
and someone who is
honest, will get the ticket.

257
00:15:53,103 --> 00:15:55,468
Our CM is visiting on the 10th...

258
00:15:55,492 --> 00:15:57,503
to inaugurate the government hospital.

259
00:15:57,528 --> 00:16:00,802
He would be meeting me
and confirming the candidate.

260
00:16:04,149 --> 00:16:06,081
[fax machine buzzing]

261
00:16:08,924 --> 00:16:11,674
How did the paper travel so
far and come out from this?

262
00:16:18,854 --> 00:16:20,525
The CM is visiting next week.

263
00:16:20,550 --> 00:16:22,592
Here are the security details
from the Commissioner's office.

264
00:16:22,616 --> 00:16:24,388
-Note everything down.
-Okay, sir.

265
00:16:24,440 --> 00:16:27,047
If you find anyone suspicious
in the town, bring them in.

266
00:16:27,072 --> 00:16:27,955
Okay, sir.

267
00:16:28,936 --> 00:16:30,382
-Give me the fax manual.
-Here you go, sir.

268
00:16:35,532 --> 00:16:37,532
[overlapping clamor]

269
00:16:43,322 --> 00:16:44,195
[knife whooshing]

270
00:16:44,219 --> 00:16:46,942
Were you a cook before, Karuna?

271
00:16:47,026 --> 00:16:47,947
No.

272
00:16:48,741 --> 00:16:51,532
I simply love chopping stuff.

273
00:16:51,574 --> 00:16:53,366
Where's the appeal in that?

274
00:16:56,437 --> 00:16:58,232
What are your plans
once you get out, Karuna?

275
00:17:05,801 --> 00:17:08,532
When I was a kid, I went
to Paderu this one time.

276
00:17:08,699 --> 00:17:11,324
There, I saw a country
hen at a butcher shop.

277
00:17:11,699 --> 00:17:14,068
It was a well-fed hen,

278
00:17:14,282 --> 00:17:16,776
living happily with its family.

279
00:17:17,199 --> 00:17:19,282
I gave it to this one family I met.

280
00:17:20,157 --> 00:17:22,544
They snapped its neck
right in front of me...

281
00:17:22,568 --> 00:17:24,156
and made chicken curry for me.

282
00:17:24,282 --> 00:17:26,616
Each mouthful was so heavenly that...

283
00:17:26,657 --> 00:17:28,816
it felt like I was consuming
every happy moment...

284
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:31,451
that the hen has had.

285
00:17:31,991 --> 00:17:33,282
Let's say I get out of here.

286
00:17:33,657 --> 00:17:36,491
I will go hunting for one such hen...

287
00:17:36,728 --> 00:17:38,062
and devour it.

288
00:17:38,115 --> 00:17:39,031
Karuna...

289
00:17:39,819 --> 00:17:42,152
-Sir.
-You have a visitor. Follow me.

290
00:17:54,282 --> 00:17:55,741
Bro, over here.

291
00:17:57,783 --> 00:18:00,107
-I saw Jhansi, bro.
-Be loud, man!

292
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:01,557
I saw Jhansi!

293
00:18:01,582 --> 00:18:02,749
[alarming music playing]

294
00:18:02,773 --> 00:18:04,690
I think it was her.

295
00:18:06,535 --> 00:18:07,251
Where did you see her?

296
00:18:07,275 --> 00:18:09,274
Near Pamara Junction,
on the Ballavaram Bus.

297
00:18:09,298 --> 00:18:10,841
I'm not sure if it was her.

298
00:18:10,906 --> 00:18:13,003
I thought I would tell you anyway.

299
00:18:14,924 --> 00:18:16,532
How long have you been under me?

300
00:18:16,556 --> 00:18:17,841
A few years now, bro.

301
00:18:17,866 --> 00:18:19,574
Have you learned nothing at all?

302
00:18:20,985 --> 00:18:23,549
What's the most important
thing to me? Huh?

303
00:18:23,620 --> 00:18:24,578
Jhansi, bro.

304
00:18:24,821 --> 00:18:26,821
When you see someone who might be her,

305
00:18:27,174 --> 00:18:30,966
don't you think you should've
followed her and confirmed...

306
00:18:31,538 --> 00:18:34,371
instead of running to
me with your suspicions?

307
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:38,544
Go back there and confirm if it's her.

308
00:18:38,568 --> 00:18:39,435
Okay, bro.

309
00:18:47,023 --> 00:18:49,336
[heavy breathing]

310
00:18:51,608 --> 00:18:53,608
[prayer bell clinking]

311
00:18:59,095 --> 00:19:00,234
[door creaks]

312
00:19:04,731 --> 00:19:06,940
[grandma praying]

313
00:19:22,490 --> 00:19:24,490
[playful music playing]

314
00:19:32,507 --> 00:19:34,674
Kamakshi, make the elder
daughter-in-law light the lamp.

315
00:19:36,507 --> 00:19:37,549
Apply vermillion.

316
00:19:38,675 --> 00:19:39,509
Here.

317
00:19:41,804 --> 00:19:44,929
Not to me. To the tulasi plant.

318
00:19:52,882 --> 00:19:53,966
Go around it.

319
00:19:53,991 --> 00:19:54,907
This is fun.

320
00:19:56,215 --> 00:19:57,174
Clockwise.

321
00:19:59,438 --> 00:20:01,324
[pleasant music playing]

322
00:20:06,827 --> 00:20:07,702
Go again.

323
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:15,410
One last time.

324
00:20:25,131 --> 00:20:27,214
Come, light the lamp.

325
00:20:29,408 --> 00:20:30,449
The lamp is down there.

326
00:20:30,595 --> 00:20:31,637
Over there.

327
00:20:38,269 --> 00:20:39,222
What!

328
00:20:39,614 --> 00:20:40,656
Oh, lord!

329
00:20:44,220 --> 00:20:45,053
Now...

330
00:20:46,679 --> 00:20:47,512
Take this.

331
00:20:49,473 --> 00:20:50,514
Light it up.

332
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:52,997
-Show it to the tulsi plant. Not me.
-I know, I know.

333
00:20:55,521 --> 00:20:56,313
Over there.

334
00:21:07,248 --> 00:21:08,542
What's going on?

335
00:21:20,874 --> 00:21:22,207
Can you sing a prayer?

336
00:21:22,930 --> 00:21:24,013
Can you?

337
00:21:27,011 --> 00:21:27,991
Go ahead then.

338
00:21:28,898 --> 00:21:30,262
Repeat after me, okay?

339
00:21:30,423 --> 00:21:32,386
[singing prayer]

340
00:21:32,411 --> 00:21:36,742
[chanting a prayer]

341
00:21:41,589 --> 00:21:42,582
How did the engagement go?

342
00:21:42,607 --> 00:21:43,931
We definitely missed you.

343
00:21:44,164 --> 00:21:46,498
-How's your dad doing now?
-He's much better.

344
00:21:46,736 --> 00:21:47,859
God bless you!

345
00:21:47,884 --> 00:21:48,926
You also do it.

346
00:21:50,040 --> 00:21:52,413
It's alright.

347
00:21:52,437 --> 00:21:54,414
It's okay.

348
00:21:55,112 --> 00:21:56,112
Stand back.

349
00:21:59,479 --> 00:22:00,433
Fold your hands.

350
00:22:22,634 --> 00:22:24,722
This is Anasuya.
Our younger son's wife.

351
00:22:24,747 --> 00:22:26,035
She's our darling.

352
00:22:27,252 --> 00:22:28,860
That's Anirudh's wife Swarna.

353
00:22:28,944 --> 00:22:29,819
Oh.

354
00:22:30,363 --> 00:22:31,435
Namaste.

355
00:22:36,883 --> 00:22:40,408
I wanted Anirudh to marry
a cultured girl like you.

356
00:22:40,769 --> 00:22:42,151
Guess I'm not that lucky.

357
00:22:44,261 --> 00:22:48,391
Watch and learn what an ideal
daughter-in-law should be like.

358
00:22:51,478 --> 00:22:54,022
I heard you put vermillion
on mom instead of the tulsi.

359
00:22:54,046 --> 00:22:55,898
It has become a hot topic.

360
00:22:56,155 --> 00:22:57,444
Arghhh, stop it!

361
00:22:57,704 --> 00:23:00,263
They were breathing down my neck.

362
00:23:00,444 --> 00:23:02,839
I broke under pressure
and got confused.

363
00:23:03,501 --> 00:23:04,747
What are you even saying?

364
00:23:04,778 --> 00:23:07,532
Stop blaming them
and check yourself first.

365
00:23:07,726 --> 00:23:09,709
I bet they sulk only in front of me.

366
00:23:09,891 --> 00:23:11,494
You should've seen them with Anasuya.

367
00:23:11,518 --> 00:23:16,376
They were smiling with
their teeth wide open.

368
00:23:17,209 --> 00:23:19,042
I just stood there like a loser.

369
00:23:21,119 --> 00:23:22,959
Why did you leave me alone at home?

370
00:23:23,334 --> 00:23:24,543
You should've woken me up.

371
00:23:25,113 --> 00:23:26,655
This is all because of you.

372
00:23:27,917 --> 00:23:30,486
Otherwise, I would've
gotten dressed up too.

373
00:23:30,843 --> 00:23:33,224
Anasuya would look pale in comparison.

374
00:23:33,249 --> 00:23:35,749
There you go! Why do you
compare yourself to her?

375
00:23:36,096 --> 00:23:39,246
She's the only one in this
house who caters to the needs...

376
00:23:39,270 --> 00:23:40,679
of every family member.

377
00:23:40,751 --> 00:23:42,417
Please don't compete with her.

378
00:23:42,710 --> 00:23:44,952
Let's just get out of
here with pass marks.

379
00:23:45,126 --> 00:23:47,959
If there's a 'Perfect
Daughter-in-Law' award, it goes to her.

380
00:23:48,435 --> 00:23:50,435
[music playing on gramophone]

381
00:23:56,209 --> 00:23:57,668
Ganga gave 3 liters of milk today,

382
00:23:57,668 --> 00:23:59,561
Ah, I missed it! You should've called me.

383
00:23:59,586 --> 00:24:01,069
Ganga wouldn't let you touch her.

384
00:24:01,417 --> 00:24:02,793
She's comfortable only with me.

385
00:24:02,818 --> 00:24:05,484
It's okay. You aren't from
here. You wouldn’t know.

386
00:24:09,959 --> 00:24:10,793
Father-in-law...

387
00:24:11,167 --> 00:24:11,876
Your coffee.

388
00:24:17,596 --> 00:24:21,728
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

389
00:24:23,497 --> 00:24:27,514
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

390
00:24:29,519 --> 00:24:31,852
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

391
00:24:31,882 --> 00:24:34,100
Sister-in-law, what have
you done to those flowers?

392
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,526
[laughs]

393
00:24:35,655 --> 00:24:38,167
It's okay, sister.
You aren't from here.

394
00:24:38,192 --> 00:24:39,147
Let me do it.

395
00:24:41,459 --> 00:24:46,668
Dhanush, stop! Just one bite, come on!

396
00:24:47,797 --> 00:24:48,820
Open your mouth.

397
00:24:49,106 --> 00:24:53,123
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

398
00:24:55,197 --> 00:24:57,176
Father-in-law, have this rasam instead.

399
00:24:58,581 --> 00:24:59,708
[smirks]

400
00:25:02,252 --> 00:25:03,377
What's wrong?

401
00:25:03,677 --> 00:25:06,373
We have piping hot rasam
straight from the stove.

402
00:25:06,410 --> 00:25:08,744
You aren't from here.
You wouldn’t know.

403
00:25:11,373 --> 00:25:12,300
[oil sizzling]

404
00:25:12,325 --> 00:25:13,684
We had 20 cooks.

405
00:25:14,251 --> 00:25:16,893
There you are! Want this?

406
00:25:16,917 --> 00:25:18,251
-Tasty, isn't it?
-Yeah.

407
00:25:18,292 --> 00:25:20,876
Your aunt Anasuya made
them. They're delicious!

408
00:25:20,905 --> 00:25:23,392
"A woman's true beauty dwells
in the hands that tend her home"

409
00:25:23,417 --> 00:25:25,042
Go on, press her feet!

410
00:25:25,084 --> 00:25:26,959
Her gold necklace is definitely yours now.

411
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,547
That gold necklace is mine
even if I don't press her feet.

412
00:25:30,584 --> 00:25:31,584
Please total it, ma'am.

413
00:25:31,609 --> 00:25:33,317
-Here you go.
-Can I do it?

414
00:25:33,463 --> 00:25:35,568
I studied BA Economics. I can do it.

415
00:25:35,880 --> 00:25:36,896
Alright, here you go.

416
00:25:36,930 --> 00:25:40,276
"Where does lasting prosperity reside?"

417
00:25:40,306 --> 00:25:42,280
"In a house that welcomes
dawn with rangoli"

418
00:25:42,305 --> 00:25:44,305
Swarna, take these inside and...

419
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:46,084
Oh, you aren't familiar.

420
00:25:46,472 --> 00:25:48,373
Anasuya, please take these inside.

421
00:25:48,398 --> 00:25:51,567
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

422
00:25:51,592 --> 00:25:55,569
"Flowers bloom and fruits ripen in
a home touched by love and grace"

423
00:25:55,594 --> 00:25:57,345
Get me one more dosa, dear.

424
00:25:59,365 --> 00:26:02,958
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

425
00:26:03,197 --> 00:26:04,135
[chair creaks]

426
00:26:04,159 --> 00:26:05,470
Dad...

427
00:26:13,467 --> 00:26:15,618
-Which way is the post office?
-That way.

428
00:26:16,620 --> 00:26:18,419
[hen cackling]

429
00:26:21,978 --> 00:26:23,194
[telephone ringing]

430
00:26:23,218 --> 00:26:25,111
(Kid) Yay! It's a new TV.

431
00:26:25,179 --> 00:26:26,959
[telephone continues ringing]

432
00:26:28,835 --> 00:26:30,459
Hello? Hello?

433
00:26:30,917 --> 00:26:32,251
What's that noise?

434
00:26:32,251 --> 00:26:34,769
I won 'The Ideal Woman' game show.

435
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:37,126
They gave me an OnidaTV.
It's getting fixed.

436
00:26:37,260 --> 00:26:39,569
You're happy, right?
That's all I want.

437
00:26:39,835 --> 00:26:41,251
Is everything alright over there?

438
00:26:41,292 --> 00:26:42,501
Not the slightest.

439
00:26:42,810 --> 00:26:44,381
Nobody here likes me.

440
00:26:44,649 --> 00:26:47,316
Relax. They will warm up to you.

441
00:26:47,883 --> 00:26:49,473
There's no time. It has to be quick.

442
00:26:50,621 --> 00:26:51,690
Why don't you come here?

443
00:26:52,011 --> 00:26:54,720
Why? What will I do there?

444
00:26:55,117 --> 00:26:57,712
There's a lady here called Anasuya,
who'd steal that award from you.

445
00:26:58,178 --> 00:27:00,252
I want to be better than her.

446
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:05,032
If you can help me with
cooking, I'll impress them.

447
00:27:05,459 --> 00:27:08,167
Are you serious?

448
00:27:08,278 --> 00:27:11,697
'The Ideal Woman' should
take care of her best friend too,

449
00:27:11,721 --> 00:27:13,084
not just the husband.

450
00:27:13,167 --> 00:27:16,793
My husband can't survive without my food.

451
00:27:16,835 --> 00:27:18,334
Please try to understand.

452
00:27:18,459 --> 00:27:20,793
Also, I have guests
over to watch the new TV.

453
00:27:20,959 --> 00:27:24,283
Alright. You enjoy cooking
and watching your new TV.

454
00:27:25,739 --> 00:27:27,578
I can't believe you've
forgotten everything.

455
00:27:28,501 --> 00:27:31,084
I thought I would also find a nice family.

456
00:27:35,042 --> 00:27:38,126
I guess I'm not destined for happiness.

457
00:27:39,334 --> 00:27:41,876
Everyone can't have
a happy family like you.

458
00:27:44,084 --> 00:27:46,709
Remember everything that I
did for you when we were kids?

459
00:27:47,007 --> 00:27:49,550
I bought ribbons and
talcum powder for you...

460
00:27:49,574 --> 00:27:51,383
with my savings at the orphanage.

461
00:27:51,408 --> 00:27:55,076
You looked so cute in those
that a couple adopted you...

462
00:27:55,100 --> 00:27:56,220
instead of me.

463
00:27:57,793 --> 00:27:59,292
Why are you digging the past now?

464
00:28:00,167 --> 00:28:01,584
It's just my fate.

465
00:28:02,340 --> 00:28:04,942
I wish I had a friend like myself.

466
00:28:04,967 --> 00:28:07,967
You're being more dramatic...

467
00:28:08,167 --> 00:28:11,668
than Sridevi and Jayaprada.

468
00:28:11,851 --> 00:28:13,851
There's a bigger drama going on here.

469
00:28:13,876 --> 00:28:15,908
I'm literally begging you, can't you see?

470
00:28:15,933 --> 00:28:17,767
Have I ever asked you for anything?

471
00:28:18,065 --> 00:28:21,648
Yes! You're always asking me something.

472
00:28:21,680 --> 00:28:23,501
I meant recently.

473
00:28:23,835 --> 00:28:25,176
Yeah, you did actually.

474
00:28:25,201 --> 00:28:27,034
What about this month?

475
00:28:27,917 --> 00:28:29,543
Just tell me if you're coming or not.

476
00:28:29,568 --> 00:28:30,777
Alright. I'll be there.

477
00:28:30,835 --> 00:28:31,959
Do I have a choice?

478
00:28:32,237 --> 00:28:33,153
Okay.

479
00:28:35,079 --> 00:28:36,496
[Husband] Hey, I'm waiting here.

480
00:28:36,557 --> 00:28:37,849
Coming, dear.

481
00:28:40,386 --> 00:28:41,833
[horn blaring]

482
00:28:41,847 --> 00:28:42,808
[thud]

483
00:28:42,832 --> 00:28:44,566
[bus comes to a halt]

484
00:28:45,307 --> 00:28:47,307
[suspenseful music playing]

485
00:28:48,835 --> 00:28:51,376
Can you make tamarind
chicken and methi mutton masala?

486
00:28:51,459 --> 00:28:55,084
I just arrived. Let me breathe.

487
00:28:55,605 --> 00:28:57,772
I'll freshen up and then get to work.

488
00:28:57,797 --> 00:28:59,593
We don't have the time.

489
00:28:59,654 --> 00:29:02,393
The wedding is soon.
My father-in-law hasn't spoken to Ani yet.

490
00:29:02,432 --> 00:29:04,965
Ani isn't saying it but he's really sad.

491
00:29:05,042 --> 00:29:07,709
I don't have a single talent
that would impress them.

492
00:29:07,959 --> 00:29:09,894
Anasuya is sweeping them away.

493
00:29:09,919 --> 00:29:11,862
Can you make tamarind chicken or not?

494
00:29:12,138 --> 00:29:15,389
It's not really tamarind
chicken but, let me handle it.

495
00:29:15,435 --> 00:29:16,681
But first, let's go home.

496
00:29:17,602 --> 00:29:20,477
-I can't take you home yet.
-Then?

497
00:29:20,760 --> 00:29:22,806
[suspenseful music playing]

498
00:29:26,334 --> 00:29:27,876
The inside is much better.

499
00:29:30,002 --> 00:29:31,211
The room is open, ma'am.

500
00:29:32,258 --> 00:29:33,069
Come.

501
00:29:34,278 --> 00:29:37,039
Are you seriously making me stay here?

502
00:29:37,107 --> 00:29:38,039
It looks nice, see?

503
00:29:38,064 --> 00:29:40,268
I hope you're kidding
because, it's disastrous!

504
00:29:40,292 --> 00:29:41,403
Be optimistic.

505
00:29:44,537 --> 00:29:45,829
It's not working.

506
00:29:48,090 --> 00:29:50,738
Now that you're here,
I know you'll fix everything.

507
00:29:50,762 --> 00:29:53,345
Of course. It's not like I have a choice.

508
00:29:53,914 --> 00:29:57,633
I'll keep you here and run the house.

509
00:29:57,922 --> 00:30:00,151
Keep me here? Sounds suggestive.

510
00:30:00,175 --> 00:30:02,339
I keep you here and run the house there.

511
00:30:02,363 --> 00:30:04,283
The word 'keep' is the problem here.

512
00:30:04,370 --> 00:30:07,912
I'll take your help and run the house.

513
00:30:08,352 --> 00:30:10,561
Anasuya will be perplexed.

514
00:30:10,641 --> 00:30:11,516
Perplexed?

515
00:30:11,549 --> 00:30:13,215
Get ready in 5 minutes.

516
00:30:13,896 --> 00:30:15,339
It's war-time.

517
00:30:15,663 --> 00:30:17,246
Let's come on!

518
00:30:20,272 --> 00:30:21,199
[sighs]

519
00:30:21,223 --> 00:30:24,890
Our village finally has a
wedding venue, all thanks to you.

520
00:30:25,012 --> 00:30:26,317
Your elder son is also in town.

521
00:30:26,346 --> 00:30:28,888
Why don't we have your
daughter's wedding here?

522
00:30:28,913 --> 00:30:29,696
Sure, why not?

523
00:30:29,721 --> 00:30:33,220
Mr. Ramaiah Raju, I heard that you
gave Kesavaiah the contesting ticket.

524
00:30:33,673 --> 00:30:34,879
It's not my individual decision.

525
00:30:34,904 --> 00:30:36,520
Don't say it's the
party leaders' decision.

526
00:30:36,713 --> 00:30:38,713
Why is it that your leaders
always seem to forget me?

527
00:30:38,742 --> 00:30:42,242
You need me for party
funds, for the votes.

528
00:30:42,441 --> 00:30:43,775
But I'm not good enough to contest.

529
00:30:43,824 --> 00:30:46,675
Aren't you supposed to check
his caliber before selecting him?

530
00:30:46,700 --> 00:30:48,991
You should take this
up at the party office.

531
00:30:49,913 --> 00:30:51,072
It's not one's caliber.

532
00:30:51,387 --> 00:30:53,012
It is one's honesty
that gets him the ticket.

533
00:30:53,037 --> 00:30:53,954
Honesty?

534
00:30:53,979 --> 00:30:54,979
We know you're a nice man.

535
00:30:55,010 --> 00:30:58,343
But your niceness only
works on the campaign posters.

536
00:30:58,368 --> 00:31:01,118
People like me to have
to all the dirty work...

537
00:31:01,217 --> 00:31:03,092
for you to get on stage
and woo the public.

538
00:31:03,117 --> 00:31:05,950
It is my money that's
fueling your political career.

539
00:31:07,855 --> 00:31:11,314
I simply came to tell you
to rethink your decision.

540
00:31:14,044 --> 00:31:15,835
Threatening is not my style, sir.

541
00:31:16,441 --> 00:31:17,649
I'm upfront about things.

542
00:31:17,817 --> 00:31:18,868
Good for you.

543
00:31:19,574 --> 00:31:21,725
My father doesn't take
threats seriously anyway.

544
00:31:22,209 --> 00:31:27,046
Considering, he hasn't looted a
single penny in these 30 years.

545
00:31:27,275 --> 00:31:28,298
That's his honesty.

546
00:31:28,332 --> 00:31:28,884
What did you say?

547
00:31:28,908 --> 00:31:31,772
Calm down, people! Step back!

548
00:31:32,759 --> 00:31:34,059
Don't engage with him.

549
00:31:34,566 --> 00:31:35,426
Let's go.

550
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:41,211
[engine revving]

551
00:31:43,325 --> 00:31:44,988
[tires screeching]

552
00:31:48,163 --> 00:31:49,516
[door clunks]

553
00:31:52,940 --> 00:31:55,065
Wash the tamarind leaves properly.

554
00:31:55,529 --> 00:31:57,112
Make sure there are no twigs.

555
00:31:58,107 --> 00:32:00,859
Add oil to the pan
and add onions,

556
00:32:00,883 --> 00:32:07,483
cinammon stick, cloves and cardamom.

557
00:32:07,508 --> 00:32:09,806
-How much are these eggplants for?
-2 rupees per kilo, ma'am.

558
00:32:09,906 --> 00:32:13,072
Oh, I almost forgot bengal gram.
That's the main ingredient.

559
00:32:13,363 --> 00:32:16,793
Oh, the one that looks
round and white in color?

560
00:32:18,702 --> 00:32:20,225
Keep these aside. I'll be right back.

561
00:32:20,250 --> 00:32:22,094
I thought you'd have the basic knowledge.

562
00:32:22,119 --> 00:32:24,413
Do I have to explain every ingredient now?

563
00:32:24,438 --> 00:32:28,605
I'll manage using cheat
sheets, like we did during exams.

564
00:32:28,630 --> 00:32:31,921
Otherwise, there's a big
tree by the kitchen window.

565
00:32:32,124 --> 00:32:34,377
You could hide behind
it and tell me what to do.

566
00:32:34,402 --> 00:32:36,583
We'll manage, don't worry.

567
00:32:39,499 --> 00:32:40,666
Be practical.

568
00:32:40,702 --> 00:32:42,368
You seriously think you can do this?

569
00:32:43,229 --> 00:32:44,229
I'll take these.

570
00:32:44,370 --> 00:32:46,745
Why do you want to cook
so desperately anyway?

571
00:32:49,648 --> 00:32:50,627
Give me two of these.

572
00:32:50,658 --> 00:32:57,325
He waited eagerly for 2 years
for his family to accept him.

573
00:32:57,927 --> 00:33:00,136
He left everyone behind for me.

574
00:33:00,639 --> 00:33:03,056
Now, shouldn't I help
him win his family back?

575
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:06,873
You know he's never asked me for anything.

576
00:33:08,035 --> 00:33:10,035
[eerie music playing]

577
00:33:18,255 --> 00:33:19,006
We need to go.

578
00:33:19,779 --> 00:33:20,530
Come, let's go!

579
00:33:20,594 --> 00:33:21,801
Where? What's wrong?

580
00:33:22,537 --> 00:33:24,454
Wow, the cucumbers are so glossy!

581
00:33:25,052 --> 00:33:27,968
Tomatoes look nice.
How much are these for?

582
00:33:27,999 --> 00:33:29,647
1 rupee per kilo, ma'am.

583
00:33:29,671 --> 00:33:30,418
Come!

584
00:33:30,443 --> 00:33:32,943
Where are you dragging me?

585
00:33:33,108 --> 00:33:35,028
[suspenseful music playing]

586
00:33:48,495 --> 00:33:49,869
Oh, you wanted fish?

587
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:55,790
That guy in checks has been following us.

588
00:33:56,328 --> 00:33:57,161
Who?

589
00:33:58,160 --> 00:33:58,920
That guy.

590
00:33:59,307 --> 00:34:02,515
Yeah, right. As if you're James Bond.

591
00:34:02,556 --> 00:34:03,683
Someone's watching too many movies.

592
00:34:04,219 --> 00:34:05,259
Let me prove it.

593
00:34:06,584 --> 00:34:08,834
Hold on. Let me get the fish.

594
00:34:09,839 --> 00:34:11,047
I can't teach you how to cook.

595
00:34:11,072 --> 00:34:13,114
Let me go back home.

596
00:34:14,327 --> 00:34:16,360
[suspenseful music intensifies]

597
00:34:17,113 --> 00:34:18,307
He is following us.

598
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:19,814
Don't look!

599
00:34:22,112 --> 00:34:23,974
Shit! He's really following us.

600
00:34:24,510 --> 00:34:25,510
What do we do now?

601
00:34:25,811 --> 00:34:26,811
I'm scared.

602
00:34:27,373 --> 00:34:29,146
I have only 10 rupees.

603
00:34:29,171 --> 00:34:30,832
He might leave if we say we have no money.

604
00:34:30,857 --> 00:34:31,908
He looks like a thief.

605
00:34:38,582 --> 00:34:39,783
No, don't do it!

606
00:34:39,807 --> 00:34:40,614
Oye!

607
00:34:42,550 --> 00:34:43,667
Why are you following us?

608
00:34:44,699 --> 00:34:46,200
I'm not following you.

609
00:34:48,732 --> 00:34:50,858
But you seem oddly familiar.

610
00:34:51,781 --> 00:34:52,865
What's your name?

611
00:34:53,580 --> 00:34:54,756
It's none of your business.

612
00:34:56,940 --> 00:34:58,441
I've definitely seen you somewhere.

613
00:34:59,685 --> 00:35:01,412
You lived in the forests
before, didn't you?

614
00:35:03,718 --> 00:35:05,286
Do you know who I am?

615
00:35:06,983 --> 00:35:09,400
Do you really know who I am?

616
00:35:11,218 --> 00:35:12,100
Jhansi?

617
00:35:14,792 --> 00:35:16,272
Get lost right now!

618
00:35:17,553 --> 00:35:20,402
If I ever see you again,

619
00:35:20,661 --> 00:35:22,490
I'll blow your brains out!

620
00:35:23,227 --> 00:35:25,173
[upbeat music playing]

621
00:35:31,868 --> 00:35:34,785
Hey! Did you just threaten him?

622
00:35:36,612 --> 00:35:38,612
Be it a hero or a housewife,

623
00:35:38,705 --> 00:35:40,758
when the dialogue lands right,

624
00:35:40,782 --> 00:35:42,688
anyone has to get scared.

625
00:35:44,016 --> 00:35:44,798
Let's go.

626
00:35:45,285 --> 00:35:48,431
You're really unpredictable sometimes.

627
00:35:49,148 --> 00:35:51,148
[crickets chirping]

628
00:36:13,947 --> 00:36:15,141
[telephone ringing]

629
00:36:16,654 --> 00:36:17,404
Sister...

630
00:36:17,482 --> 00:36:19,108
Swarna, is everything okay?

631
00:36:19,375 --> 00:36:20,848
Is he still in jail?

632
00:36:21,950 --> 00:36:24,751
He's been charged for multiple assaults.
He won't come out anytime soon.

633
00:36:25,853 --> 00:36:26,770
Why do you ask?

634
00:36:27,109 --> 00:36:27,984
Nothing.

635
00:36:28,009 --> 00:36:29,509
Swarna, be honest.

636
00:36:29,678 --> 00:36:31,977
I was just getting an update. That's all.

637
00:36:32,002 --> 00:36:33,791
Swarna, listen to me.

638
00:36:33,898 --> 00:36:35,898
[upbeat music playing]

639
00:36:36,803 --> 00:36:39,040
I came to get water.

640
00:36:40,143 --> 00:36:41,580
There's a water pot in your room.

641
00:36:41,698 --> 00:36:42,779
It's empty.

642
00:36:44,906 --> 00:36:46,406
I only filled it last night.

643
00:36:46,911 --> 00:36:48,213
Due to the extreme heat here,

644
00:36:48,718 --> 00:36:50,441
I drank it all.

645
00:36:51,048 --> 00:36:52,590
I'm not from here, remember?

646
00:36:53,315 --> 00:36:55,315
[upbeat music continues]

647
00:37:01,682 --> 00:37:05,183
Something feels off with Swarna.

648
00:37:06,348 --> 00:37:09,022
You're skeptical about
everyone but yourself.

649
00:37:09,047 --> 00:37:09,936
Now go to bed.

650
00:37:13,988 --> 00:37:15,561
[temple bell rings]

651
00:37:15,854 --> 00:37:19,104
Why is the sky draped in blue?

652
00:37:19,436 --> 00:37:21,936
Because red would’ve ruined its beauty.

653
00:37:22,182 --> 00:37:25,873
If you deny I am a poet,
I’ll answer with a blade.

654
00:37:25,898 --> 00:37:30,106
Deny me as a writer,
and I’ll answer with stones.

655
00:37:30,135 --> 00:37:31,676
Who's this poet, girl?

656
00:37:32,740 --> 00:37:33,824
Vagdevi?

657
00:37:34,030 --> 00:37:34,823
[smirks]

658
00:37:34,847 --> 00:37:36,172
Stupid stuff!

659
00:37:36,197 --> 00:37:37,739
Geetha, where's Ani?

660
00:37:39,422 --> 00:37:40,546
Where is he?

661
00:37:40,658 --> 00:37:42,678
He went to the medical
camp early morning.

662
00:37:42,702 --> 00:37:44,200
He even skipped breakfast.

663
00:37:56,450 --> 00:37:58,242
-Here you go, doctor.
-The fee is only one rupee, grandpa.

664
00:37:58,630 --> 00:38:00,103
Don't forget to take these medicines.

665
00:38:00,128 --> 00:38:01,248
Ani...

666
00:38:05,986 --> 00:38:08,736
Did you forget me and breakfast for this?

667
00:38:10,751 --> 00:38:12,792
Are there no other
doctors in this village?

668
00:38:13,490 --> 00:38:15,886
Well, there are no specialists.

669
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:19,128
So I try to do whatever I
can every time I'm here.

670
00:38:19,462 --> 00:38:23,716
Wow! You're overflowing with kindness.

671
00:38:24,276 --> 00:38:26,527
How can somebody be so nice?

672
00:38:26,946 --> 00:38:28,988
There's got to be a catch, right?

673
00:38:29,773 --> 00:38:30,730
You're the catch.

674
00:38:32,302 --> 00:38:33,093
You're right.

675
00:38:33,656 --> 00:38:35,763
Hi, doctor. How's your father doing?

676
00:38:35,788 --> 00:38:38,496
Yeah, he's fine. I'll be
right there. Please sit.

677
00:38:39,237 --> 00:38:41,691
The whole village
worships your dad, isn't it?

678
00:38:43,890 --> 00:38:46,191
But he doesn't like me.

679
00:38:46,652 --> 00:38:48,381
He hasn't said a word to me till now.

680
00:38:48,406 --> 00:38:51,026
So what? Why don't you go talk to him?

681
00:38:54,984 --> 00:38:57,818
Everything will be sorted
from tomorrow. Trust me.

682
00:38:58,685 --> 00:39:00,607
[birds chirping]

683
00:39:04,742 --> 00:39:06,781
[dramatic music playing]

684
00:39:10,768 --> 00:39:13,393
Savory doughnuts,
sweet pie, tamarind rice,

685
00:39:13,418 --> 00:39:16,876
tamarind chicken, methi
mutton masala, fish curry.

686
00:39:16,901 --> 00:39:18,984
Who made all these, mom?

687
00:39:19,009 --> 00:39:21,748
Why so many dishes?

688
00:39:21,772 --> 00:39:23,009
When did she wake up?

689
00:39:23,034 --> 00:39:23,921
What's happening?

690
00:39:23,945 --> 00:39:25,858
Why did you make so many dishes?

691
00:39:25,883 --> 00:39:27,071
Did you even sleep?

692
00:39:27,283 --> 00:39:28,449
I didn't make these, mother-in-law.

693
00:39:28,474 --> 00:39:29,611
Who did then?

694
00:39:30,332 --> 00:39:32,083
I have no clue.

695
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,255
Sister-in-law!

696
00:39:38,836 --> 00:39:40,045
Was it you?

697
00:39:40,154 --> 00:39:41,821
When did you find the
time to make all this?

698
00:39:41,846 --> 00:39:44,138
I woke up at 3 AM.

699
00:39:44,538 --> 00:39:49,218
I thought I'd make a little
something for the feast today.

700
00:39:49,243 --> 00:39:51,576
My mouth is watering
from just smelling it.

701
00:39:51,601 --> 00:39:53,018
How did you do it? My god!

702
00:39:54,765 --> 00:39:57,182
It's no small feat to
pull off a feast like this.

703
00:39:57,941 --> 00:40:00,857
I know. You must have worked so hard.

704
00:40:03,115 --> 00:40:05,961
Chicken curry, brinjal
curry, ridge gourd chutney.

705
00:40:05,986 --> 00:40:06,861
Let's kill it!

706
00:40:13,608 --> 00:40:14,400
Let's go.

707
00:40:24,343 --> 00:40:27,984
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

708
00:40:28,009 --> 00:40:31,746
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

709
00:40:31,765 --> 00:40:35,450
"Flowers bloom and fruits ripen in a home

710
00:40:35,474 --> 00:40:39,175
Touched by love and grace"

711
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:42,954
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

712
00:40:42,988 --> 00:40:46,725
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

713
00:40:52,862 --> 00:40:55,362
-She gave 4 litres of milk.
-Ganga let you touch her?

714
00:40:56,213 --> 00:40:57,782
You're awesome!

715
00:41:00,008 --> 00:41:01,353
Ganga, how could you!

716
00:41:04,556 --> 00:41:07,951
-Now, would you take a look at that!
-You like it?

717
00:41:09,259 --> 00:41:12,652
-Grandma, come with me!
-Where are you taking me?

718
00:41:12,746 --> 00:41:13,787
Come!

719
00:41:14,544 --> 00:41:22,088
"The sacred tulasi in the
courtyard rewards blessings untold"

720
00:41:22,240 --> 00:41:26,961
"The sacred tulasi in the
courtyard rewards blessings untold"

721
00:41:26,986 --> 00:41:28,319
How long is it going to take?

722
00:41:29,243 --> 00:41:30,129
Have some patience.

723
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:32,199
-Do it properly.
-You do it!

724
00:41:32,224 --> 00:41:33,219
Never mind.

725
00:41:36,700 --> 00:41:39,075
Let's start. 1..2..3!

726
00:41:39,107 --> 00:41:41,900
"The gentle cow fills the home
with plenty and well-being"

727
00:41:41,924 --> 00:41:43,216
I can't do this.

728
00:41:44,186 --> 00:41:45,977
No, no. Keep going.

729
00:41:46,258 --> 00:41:47,235
My back is killing me!

730
00:41:48,450 --> 00:41:52,289
"Pearl-like turmeric
lends a glow to her face"

731
00:41:52,311 --> 00:41:54,166
"The vermilion she wears blesses her days"

732
00:41:54,191 --> 00:41:55,792
[whispers] Did you make
gongura prawns well?

733
00:41:55,817 --> 00:41:57,276
I nailed it. Here you go.

734
00:42:01,930 --> 00:42:05,494
Mom, here's dad's BP medicine.

735
00:42:06,571 --> 00:42:09,279
These work better. I switched them up.

736
00:42:31,783 --> 00:42:34,034
Cooking everyday, rangolis and puja...

737
00:42:34,284 --> 00:42:36,325
You're on to something big.

738
00:42:37,113 --> 00:42:38,030
Hell, yeah!

739
00:42:38,447 --> 00:42:39,922
I dare you to figure it out.

740
00:42:43,150 --> 00:42:44,514
[door creaking]

741
00:42:46,679 --> 00:42:48,513
We'll be in trouble if sir finds out.

742
00:42:48,554 --> 00:42:50,221
It's okay. Relax. He's a good guy.

743
00:42:50,221 --> 00:42:51,356
He never makes any demands.

744
00:42:51,381 --> 00:42:52,214
You carry on.

745
00:42:57,804 --> 00:42:59,096
Bro, it's me.

746
00:42:59,388 --> 00:43:00,430
What's the matter?

747
00:43:00,596 --> 00:43:02,305
She's nothing like you described.

748
00:43:02,721 --> 00:43:05,596
She's like any other homemaker.

749
00:43:05,721 --> 00:43:07,929
She seems like her but
not her at the same time.

750
00:43:07,971 --> 00:43:09,305
It's totally confusing, bro!

751
00:43:09,388 --> 00:43:11,013
Give me more details.

752
00:43:11,986 --> 00:43:14,111
Have you ever dealt with someone?

753
00:43:14,513 --> 00:43:16,305
Of course, I do deals all the time.

754
00:43:18,466 --> 00:43:20,924
-Have you taken someone out before?
-Oh, like a date?

755
00:43:21,430 --> 00:43:22,897
Have you killed before?

756
00:43:22,922 --> 00:43:26,172
Oh, you mean 'kill' someone.

757
00:43:26,376 --> 00:43:27,917
You know that builder. Somaraju.

758
00:43:28,138 --> 00:43:30,651
Srinu and I killed him together.

759
00:43:30,676 --> 00:43:32,259
I struck him first though.

760
00:43:32,929 --> 00:43:34,346
Then do one thing.

761
00:43:34,388 --> 00:43:36,721
Go to the market and
ask for a country knife.

762
00:43:36,804 --> 00:43:39,763
Then stab her to death with it.

763
00:43:41,804 --> 00:43:43,221
I'm not sure if it's her.

764
00:43:44,230 --> 00:43:47,272
If you manage to kill
her, then it's not Jhansi.

765
00:43:51,554 --> 00:43:53,180
What if it is Jhansi?

766
00:43:53,221 --> 00:43:54,221
You'll be dead.

767
00:43:54,386 --> 00:43:55,968
Your guy is crazy mad!

768
00:43:57,309 --> 00:43:58,449
Don't mix everything up.

769
00:44:00,721 --> 00:44:05,221
I prayed that I'd visit Venkatapuram
temple if her marriage is fixed.

770
00:44:05,493 --> 00:44:08,535
No one seems to care enough to take me.

771
00:44:08,821 --> 00:44:11,113
Everyone's busy with the wedding chores.

772
00:44:11,727 --> 00:44:13,727
All the men have their respective tasks.

773
00:44:13,841 --> 00:44:17,966
Everyone gets their
works done, except for me.

774
00:44:18,637 --> 00:44:23,096
Hey! I can't watch someone
be sad when I'm in this house.

775
00:44:23,313 --> 00:44:27,355
I know everyone from the
valet to the priest at that temple.

776
00:44:27,472 --> 00:44:28,804
They will give us a VIP experience.

777
00:44:28,959 --> 00:44:30,971
Be ready first thing in the morning.

778
00:44:31,049 --> 00:44:34,091
I'll take you people directly
to the God's chamber.

779
00:44:34,385 --> 00:44:36,178
[birds chirping]

780
00:44:43,810 --> 00:44:44,810
We've reached. Get down.

781
00:44:44,976 --> 00:44:46,184
Get down, mother-in-law.

782
00:44:49,434 --> 00:44:50,393
Careful.

783
00:44:51,108 --> 00:44:53,108
[doors shut]

784
00:44:54,399 --> 00:44:55,735
Swarna, let's go.

785
00:44:55,760 --> 00:44:57,882
See, I made it happen.

786
00:44:58,269 --> 00:45:00,671
Hey, look! That's Buchiraju, isn't it?

787
00:45:00,696 --> 00:45:02,820
-Who's Buchiraju?
-Ramaiah Raju's son-in-law.

788
00:45:02,976 --> 00:45:04,789
How dare they mess with us?

789
00:45:04,813 --> 00:45:06,187
Let's go get him.

790
00:45:07,028 --> 00:45:08,195
Guys, let's go.

791
00:45:08,219 --> 00:45:10,131
[eerie music playing]

792
00:45:11,311 --> 00:45:12,179
[oil sizzling]

793
00:45:12,203 --> 00:45:12,995
Hey!

794
00:45:13,282 --> 00:45:14,574
Didn't you go to the temple?

795
00:45:15,315 --> 00:45:19,440
Your sister-in-law is somehow
cooking everything before I wake up.

796
00:45:19,684 --> 00:45:22,058
So before they return from the temple,

797
00:45:22,177 --> 00:45:25,886
I'm going to cook everything
and impress them.

798
00:45:26,761 --> 00:45:27,803
Wait, don't I get a coffee?

799
00:45:28,010 --> 00:45:29,094
Have it at the station.

800
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:32,753
[devotional song
playing in the background]

801
00:45:35,213 --> 00:45:37,213
[eerie music continues]

802
00:45:45,264 --> 00:45:46,431
Go ahead and pray, sister-in-law.

803
00:46:28,450 --> 00:46:30,423
[upbeat music playing]

804
00:46:49,205 --> 00:46:50,355
Come, take the harathi (blessings).

805
00:46:54,032 --> 00:46:56,120
-Let's go?
-Yeah. Let's move.

806
00:46:56,144 --> 00:46:59,330
Hurry up! We got to be
home before father-in-law.

807
00:47:06,072 --> 00:47:09,199
-Let's go, let's go.
-Stop rushing us, Buchiraju.

808
00:47:09,224 --> 00:47:10,683
The car is that way.

809
00:47:13,006 --> 00:47:14,079
Bro, two soda.

810
00:47:14,449 --> 00:47:15,242
Here you go.

811
00:47:15,612 --> 00:47:16,399
For them.

812
00:47:19,704 --> 00:47:21,677
[upbeat music intensifies]

813
00:47:25,243 --> 00:47:27,183
[soda cart rattling]

814
00:47:27,230 --> 00:47:29,149
[explosion]

815
00:47:32,802 --> 00:47:34,694
[upbeat music continues]

816
00:47:40,484 --> 00:47:44,019
-They're here to kill us!
-Get in! Hurry up!

817
00:47:44,043 --> 00:47:45,376
There they are! Catch them!

818
00:47:47,480 --> 00:47:48,332
Start the car!

819
00:47:48,357 --> 00:47:49,436
Where's the key?

820
00:47:49,467 --> 00:47:51,202
Get in quickly, guys!

821
00:47:51,227 --> 00:47:52,249
Get in.

822
00:47:52,274 --> 00:47:53,732
I said, get in!

823
00:47:55,142 --> 00:47:57,354
Get in! Let's go!

824
00:47:57,852 --> 00:47:59,686
Guys, stop the car!

825
00:47:59,730 --> 00:48:01,243
[gear shifts]

826
00:48:01,345 --> 00:48:02,499
Where are you going?

827
00:48:02,510 --> 00:48:03,996
[thud]

828
00:48:04,183 --> 00:48:05,122
[gear shifts]

829
00:48:05,147 --> 00:48:06,031
[engine revs]

830
00:48:06,055 --> 00:48:08,457
I told you to go back.
Why did you crash the bike?

831
00:48:09,001 --> 00:48:10,664
Never mind. That was a nice move.

832
00:48:10,738 --> 00:48:11,904
[engine revs]

833
00:48:14,566 --> 00:48:15,946
[bikes revving]

834
00:48:21,187 --> 00:48:23,020
You said you'd take
care of everything.

835
00:48:23,061 --> 00:48:24,187
What do you have to say now?

836
00:48:24,228 --> 00:48:27,264
You were the one who wanted to
visit the temple. Don't blame me now.

837
00:48:27,289 --> 00:48:29,748
-I didn't know you could drive.
-I can wing it.

838
00:48:30,087 --> 00:48:31,212
Wing it?

839
00:48:32,008 --> 00:48:33,277
[yelling]

840
00:48:33,301 --> 00:48:35,663
Son-in-law, why are
these goons chasing us?

841
00:48:35,763 --> 00:48:37,286
We shouldn't have stepped out.

842
00:48:37,311 --> 00:48:38,894
I don't have such violent enemies.

843
00:48:38,919 --> 00:48:41,083
They're catching up!

844
00:48:41,107 --> 00:48:42,879
[bikes revving]

845
00:48:49,580 --> 00:48:51,580
[music intensifies]

846
00:48:52,153 --> 00:48:53,092
[car engine revs]

847
00:48:53,116 --> 00:48:53,951
Keep going.

848
00:48:54,039 --> 00:48:55,179
[thud]

849
00:48:58,000 --> 00:48:59,747
Swarna, careful.

850
00:48:59,758 --> 00:49:01,691
[upbeat music playing]

851
00:49:02,948 --> 00:49:04,584
He pulled out a gun!

852
00:49:04,608 --> 00:49:06,714
He's stuck on the
windshield like a lizard.

853
00:49:06,803 --> 00:49:08,103
[bikes revving]

854
00:49:12,157 --> 00:49:13,703
[screams]

855
00:49:15,133 --> 00:49:16,684
What if we all die here?

856
00:49:16,708 --> 00:49:18,447
There's no female at home to mourn us.

857
00:49:18,472 --> 00:49:20,502
What are you saying?
Anasuya is home only, dear.

858
00:49:20,782 --> 00:49:21,782
Focus there.

859
00:49:21,924 --> 00:49:23,105
Watch out!

860
00:49:24,949 --> 00:49:28,325
Geetha, take the coconut and
wrap a cloth around it tightly.

861
00:49:28,381 --> 00:49:29,494
Alright, alright.

862
00:49:30,347 --> 00:49:32,422
Have you ever catapulted
a stone at a mango tree?

863
00:49:32,422 --> 00:49:33,297
Got it, got it.

864
00:49:34,416 --> 00:49:36,784
They're close. We need to do something.

865
00:49:37,215 --> 00:49:39,283
Hit him! Go for it!

866
00:49:39,308 --> 00:49:42,802
Just do it! You got this!

867
00:49:42,893 --> 00:49:43,966
[grunts]

868
00:49:44,634 --> 00:49:45,577
Watch out!

869
00:49:45,601 --> 00:49:48,918
Just swing it at him! Do it!

870
00:49:48,943 --> 00:49:49,791
[thud]

871
00:49:50,018 --> 00:49:51,165
[screams]

872
00:49:52,149 --> 00:49:54,649
-[Geetha screaming]
-He has a knife!

873
00:49:54,977 --> 00:49:56,663
[knife whooshes]

874
00:49:56,946 --> 00:49:57,826
Careful.

875
00:49:57,851 --> 00:49:59,089
[door clunks]

876
00:49:59,114 --> 00:50:00,189
[screams]

877
00:50:02,502 --> 00:50:03,752
Good-riddance!

878
00:50:05,834 --> 00:50:07,907
What the hell! They're on to us again.

879
00:50:07,932 --> 00:50:09,361
They're overtaking us from that side.

880
00:50:13,337 --> 00:50:15,809
They should forget all about
Swarna once they taste this.

881
00:50:15,834 --> 00:50:19,480
Swarna, they're so close.

882
00:50:19,535 --> 00:50:20,908
[bike revs]

883
00:50:20,981 --> 00:50:22,174
[tires screeching]

884
00:50:22,199 --> 00:50:23,268
[thud]

885
00:50:27,595 --> 00:50:29,297
-They're all down! Thank god!
-No, they're not.

886
00:50:29,321 --> 00:50:30,478
Two guys are charging from the front.

887
00:50:30,503 --> 00:50:31,472
Be ready.

888
00:50:33,395 --> 00:50:34,355
They're close.

889
00:50:34,854 --> 00:50:35,755
Open the door!

890
00:50:36,063 --> 00:50:37,290
[doors clunk]

891
00:50:37,603 --> 00:50:38,851
[thud]

892
00:50:38,875 --> 00:50:39,916
[groans]

893
00:50:42,590 --> 00:50:43,924
The last guy is down too!

894
00:50:44,682 --> 00:50:46,057
You were awesome, sister-in-law!

895
00:50:46,420 --> 00:50:47,754
You drove well.

896
00:50:48,442 --> 00:50:49,650
We almost reached our village.

897
00:50:50,300 --> 00:50:51,592
Should I take the wheel from here?

898
00:50:53,287 --> 00:50:54,870
We're almost home, so...

899
00:50:55,484 --> 00:50:59,019
Buchiraju, you must be
really tired from being so afraid.

900
00:51:01,259 --> 00:51:03,217
One of our girls is about to get married.

901
00:51:03,623 --> 00:51:05,590
You should've checked with me...

902
00:51:05,684 --> 00:51:08,326
before visiting such a far-off temple.

903
00:51:09,644 --> 00:51:10,338
Mom...

904
00:51:11,098 --> 00:51:12,556
Did you come up with this plan?

905
00:51:13,806 --> 00:51:16,265
Grandma told us to ask you first.

906
00:51:17,140 --> 00:51:19,721
But Buchiraju said he's got this.

907
00:51:20,627 --> 00:51:22,794
And that we would be back in no time.

908
00:51:38,504 --> 00:51:39,546
Trust me when I say this.

909
00:51:39,571 --> 00:51:40,939
We wouldn't be alive
if it weren't for her.

910
00:51:40,964 --> 00:51:42,006
Sorry.

911
00:51:42,346 --> 00:51:45,302
See, he didn't say anything
because you're the son-in-law.

912
00:51:45,327 --> 00:51:47,628
If it were someone else,
he'd have lashed out at them.

913
00:51:47,653 --> 00:51:51,425
I know you'd rather take it
upon yourself than see us sad.

914
00:51:54,117 --> 00:51:55,075
Just a minute.

915
00:51:56,007 --> 00:51:57,507
I have a doubt.

916
00:51:57,573 --> 00:51:59,255
Did you think of this beforehand

917
00:51:59,279 --> 00:52:01,115
or come up with it on the spot?

918
00:52:01,312 --> 00:52:03,259
Did I have the luxury
of thinking it through?

919
00:52:03,369 --> 00:52:04,869
I came up with it on the spot.

920
00:52:06,208 --> 00:52:07,385
[telephone clicks]

921
00:52:08,334 --> 00:52:09,774
DSP sir can't do anything.

922
00:52:10,091 --> 00:52:11,401
They aren't even dacoits.

923
00:52:11,935 --> 00:52:14,293
I'm sure Madhusudhan Rao is behind this.

924
00:52:14,318 --> 00:52:16,126
[eerie music playing]

925
00:52:18,731 --> 00:52:19,634
Guess what!

926
00:52:19,658 --> 00:52:22,153
I made your favorite
prawns fry and biryani.

927
00:52:22,178 --> 00:52:23,093
It tastes too good.

928
00:52:23,118 --> 00:52:25,335
That can wait. You know
what happened today?

929
00:52:25,452 --> 00:52:29,116
Swarna drove the car like a pro.
She went vroom vroom.

930
00:52:29,141 --> 00:52:30,902
I made your favorite fish curry, grandma.

931
00:52:30,943 --> 00:52:33,730
We wouldn't have made it without Swarna.

932
00:52:33,768 --> 00:52:34,684
Mother-in-law!

933
00:52:35,710 --> 00:52:37,624
I made your favorite chicken pulao.

934
00:52:38,008 --> 00:52:38,924
I'll taste it in a bit.

935
00:52:39,526 --> 00:52:40,903
-Sravani...
-Mom.

936
00:52:40,928 --> 00:52:43,595
-Call Ani and Swarna to my room.
-Okay, mom.

937
00:52:45,057 --> 00:52:46,154
There's more.

938
00:52:48,815 --> 00:52:49,565
Listen, dear.

939
00:52:51,128 --> 00:52:54,753
I want to pass on the necklace
mother-in-law gave me, to Swarna.

940
00:52:56,063 --> 00:52:58,036
I should've done it when
they first got married.

941
00:52:58,550 --> 00:52:59,633
I guess it's never too late.

942
00:53:02,006 --> 00:53:04,799
He may have married
someone you didn't approve of.

943
00:53:05,606 --> 00:53:07,443
But she's definitely a good person.

944
00:53:09,703 --> 00:53:10,579
Alright.

945
00:53:10,600 --> 00:53:12,600
[cheerful music playing]

946
00:53:14,456 --> 00:53:16,129
When did you learn to drive?

947
00:53:16,274 --> 00:53:18,270
I learned as I kept driving.

948
00:53:18,539 --> 00:53:20,590
I drove as I kept learning.

949
00:53:28,988 --> 00:53:31,800
This is a family heirloom passed
on to the first daughter-in-law.

950
00:53:33,421 --> 00:53:34,864
I know it's long overdue.

951
00:53:35,153 --> 00:53:36,320
Well, it's finally time.

952
00:53:38,653 --> 00:53:41,722
-See how she impressed her.
-Hmm.

953
00:53:41,747 --> 00:53:44,224
Her and everyone else.

954
00:53:44,249 --> 00:53:45,499
Try it on, love.

955
00:53:45,657 --> 00:53:47,344
It will look beautiful on you.

956
00:53:55,421 --> 00:53:57,311
They're all such nice people.

957
00:53:57,806 --> 00:54:00,431
It feels wrong to deceive them.

958
00:54:01,034 --> 00:54:03,410
Oh. So you're going
to tell them the truth?

959
00:54:06,093 --> 00:54:10,343
Or I could fully transform
into the Swarna they think I am.

960
00:54:11,719 --> 00:54:14,071
That way, I wouldn't have to
tell them the truth anymore.

961
00:54:15,457 --> 00:54:19,706
Please teach me all the recipes
you know quickly. Chop, chop!

962
00:54:20,921 --> 00:54:22,283
Chop, chop?

963
00:54:23,044 --> 00:54:26,654
[dramatically] It's many generations
of knowledge and years of practice.

964
00:54:26,751 --> 00:54:27,918
Do you think this is a joke?

965
00:54:28,127 --> 00:54:30,877
Cooking is a form of penance
performed in front of the stove.

966
00:54:30,902 --> 00:54:34,506
Your eyes and hands should
burn, you must shed blood.

967
00:54:34,668 --> 00:54:36,418
Have you ever seen blood at least?

968
00:54:36,968 --> 00:54:37,843
I thought so!

969
00:54:38,526 --> 00:54:43,317
Only then you can make these
traditional recipes you dream of.

970
00:54:44,103 --> 00:54:45,231
Is there so much to it?

971
00:54:45,751 --> 00:54:49,205
Alright. Teach me at least
one recipe in your style.

972
00:54:50,010 --> 00:54:53,802
Not happening. I'll teach
you something in your style.

973
00:54:53,835 --> 00:54:54,808
Thanks.

974
00:54:54,922 --> 00:54:56,477
[crickets chirping]

975
00:54:58,840 --> 00:55:00,840
[door creaks]

976
00:55:02,686 --> 00:55:04,145
I'll learn this recipe as well.

977
00:55:04,270 --> 00:55:07,603
There's still time for that.
Take this inside for now.

978
00:55:08,898 --> 00:55:10,379
[door creaks]

979
00:55:14,773 --> 00:55:16,869
It's the last house over there.

980
00:55:22,290 --> 00:55:24,388
Who is it at this time of the night?

981
00:55:24,448 --> 00:55:26,218
[scooter engine revving]

982
00:55:29,129 --> 00:55:31,212
[scooter engine revving]

983
00:55:37,018 --> 00:55:38,674
-Are you scared?
-Shut up!

984
00:55:38,924 --> 00:55:40,799
So many guys to kill one woman?

985
00:55:41,020 --> 00:55:43,020
-Aren't I enough?
-Just shut up!

986
00:55:43,101 --> 00:55:44,726
The job should be done
today no matter what.

987
00:55:44,802 --> 00:55:46,466
Otherwise Karuna will kill us!

988
00:55:46,727 --> 00:55:48,770
Guys, come on!

989
00:55:48,805 --> 00:55:50,456
[eerie music playing]

990
00:55:54,194 --> 00:55:55,378
[metal clunks]

991
00:56:04,433 --> 00:56:06,683
Let's sneak into the house slowly.

992
00:56:07,282 --> 00:56:08,889
It's her, guys. Hide.

993
00:56:19,812 --> 00:56:21,644
Let me ask her once again.

994
00:56:22,715 --> 00:56:23,757
Jhansi!

995
00:56:27,951 --> 00:56:28,826
Jhansi!

996
00:56:30,259 --> 00:56:32,133
Why is he cat-calling
her instead of attacking?

997
00:56:32,157 --> 00:56:34,407
Apparently, if he's able
to kill her, she's not Jhansi.

998
00:56:34,885 --> 00:56:36,260
What if it is Jhansi?

999
00:56:36,773 --> 00:56:37,960
Then apparently, he will die.

1000
00:56:37,993 --> 00:56:40,284
Guys, stop chatting and get to business.

1001
00:56:40,649 --> 00:56:42,649
[eerie music builds up]

1002
00:56:48,764 --> 00:56:49,847
Jhansi!

1003
00:56:50,264 --> 00:56:51,764
Are you Jhansi or not?

1004
00:56:51,806 --> 00:56:52,652
Answer me!

1005
00:56:53,305 --> 00:56:54,648
You're back?

1006
00:56:54,971 --> 00:56:56,146
Who the hell are you, man?

1007
00:56:56,910 --> 00:56:58,430
I'm asking you one last time.

1008
00:56:58,565 --> 00:56:59,942
Are you Jhansi or not?

1009
00:57:00,940 --> 00:57:03,023
Say yes, and I'll leave.

1010
00:57:03,514 --> 00:57:05,909
Otherwise, I'd have to kill you.

1011
00:57:05,925 --> 00:57:07,746
[suspenseful music playing]

1012
00:57:08,887 --> 00:57:10,381
[thud]

1013
00:57:10,405 --> 00:57:11,640
[knife whooshes]

1014
00:57:11,664 --> 00:57:13,577
[screams]

1015
00:57:16,495 --> 00:57:17,769
[thud]

1016
00:57:21,427 --> 00:57:22,680
I think that's Jhansi.

1017
00:57:26,329 --> 00:57:27,492
[thud]

1018
00:57:29,559 --> 00:57:30,657
[thud sounds continue]

1019
00:57:38,900 --> 00:57:40,221
She's definitely Jhansi.

1020
00:57:40,246 --> 00:57:42,204
What are you guys looking at? Come on!

1021
00:57:47,000 --> 00:57:48,163
[thud sounds continue]

1022
00:57:55,095 --> 00:57:56,295
Who are you guys?

1023
00:57:56,680 --> 00:57:57,772
Get the hell out of here!

1024
00:58:04,539 --> 00:58:06,213
[groaning]

1025
00:58:07,597 --> 00:58:09,174
Shush!

1026
00:58:25,652 --> 00:58:27,015
[thud]

1027
00:58:29,109 --> 00:58:30,372
[groans]

1028
00:58:30,396 --> 00:58:33,246
What are you still
doing here? Get lost!

1029
00:58:34,360 --> 00:58:35,236
Hey!

1030
00:58:36,431 --> 00:58:38,833
If you ever show me your face again,

1031
00:58:38,857 --> 00:58:39,972
I'll kill you!

1032
00:58:40,226 --> 00:58:41,293
Take him away!

1033
00:58:42,974 --> 00:58:44,654
[groaning continues]

1034
00:58:45,941 --> 00:58:46,900
Get out of here!

1035
00:58:47,678 --> 00:58:48,636
Bugger off!

1036
00:58:49,559 --> 00:58:51,489
[scooter revs]

1037
00:58:51,513 --> 00:58:52,637
Damn it!

1038
00:58:58,697 --> 00:59:01,822
It's okay. At least she spared our lives.

1039
00:59:02,605 --> 00:59:03,590
[grunts]

1040
00:59:05,273 --> 00:59:06,638
I'll get my revenge.

1041
00:59:09,750 --> 00:59:10,917
Don't be an idiot.

1042
00:59:12,271 --> 00:59:13,520
You're hopeless, man.

1043
00:59:15,540 --> 00:59:16,607
[door creaks open]

1044
00:59:16,632 --> 00:59:17,955
[knife whooshes]

1045
00:59:20,281 --> 00:59:22,219
[thud]

1046
00:59:38,006 --> 00:59:40,006
[music intensifies]

1047
00:59:46,314 --> 00:59:47,248
Swarna!

1048
00:59:49,869 --> 00:59:51,529
Gongura mutton...

1049
00:59:52,048 --> 00:59:53,248
[body thuds]

1050
01:00:00,601 --> 01:00:01,684
Kiranmayi.

1051
01:00:02,982 --> 01:00:03,899
Wake up!

1052
01:00:10,129 --> 01:00:12,055
[sharp breathing]

1053
01:00:12,581 --> 01:00:13,653
Kiranmayi.

1054
01:00:14,383 --> 01:00:15,460
Kiranmayi.

1055
01:00:18,605 --> 01:00:19,355
Kiranmayi.

1056
01:00:20,520 --> 01:00:21,475
Kiranmayi.

1057
01:00:22,278 --> 01:00:25,193
It's okay. Nothing happened.
You're fine.

1058
01:00:25,218 --> 01:00:28,810
Keep breathing. Keep breathing.

1059
01:00:28,835 --> 01:00:29,710
Slowly.

1060
01:00:29,735 --> 01:00:33,485
How can I breathe with a
dead body in front of me?

1061
01:00:33,510 --> 01:00:35,385
Shhh! Slowly.

1062
01:00:35,410 --> 01:00:39,452
Listen to me. Everything
is absolutely fine.

1063
01:00:40,717 --> 01:00:41,634
Hey!

1064
01:00:42,553 --> 01:00:43,636
Now...

1065
01:00:44,934 --> 01:00:47,351
The thief who followed us at the market,

1066
01:00:47,376 --> 01:00:48,585
he sneaked into the home.

1067
01:00:48,610 --> 01:00:50,087
So what? You'll kill him?

1068
01:00:50,112 --> 01:00:51,028
Keep it low.

1069
01:00:51,469 --> 01:00:53,970
I didn't kill him.
He caused his own death.

1070
01:00:54,711 --> 01:00:58,628
How is it possible that he came
home and caused his own death?

1071
01:00:58,961 --> 01:00:59,945
He's been stabbed.

1072
01:00:59,970 --> 01:01:02,344
Oh, no! I didn't stab him.

1073
01:01:02,638 --> 01:01:04,728
His knife stabbed him only.

1074
01:01:04,979 --> 01:01:08,187
How can an inanimate object stab him?

1075
01:01:09,171 --> 01:01:13,472
So, he came running.

1076
01:01:13,680 --> 01:01:14,972
He sprained his ankle,

1077
01:01:15,931 --> 01:01:17,722
fell on the knife and died.

1078
01:01:17,747 --> 01:01:19,997
Which exactly means you killed him.

1079
01:01:20,704 --> 01:01:21,845
You're not getting it.

1080
01:01:22,935 --> 01:01:23,852
Look at me.

1081
01:01:24,693 --> 01:01:25,901
I was walking.

1082
01:01:26,080 --> 01:01:28,080
He came on to me like this.

1083
01:01:28,683 --> 01:01:31,850
And then he slipped
and fell on his own knife.

1084
01:01:33,115 --> 01:01:34,740
Will you help me or not?

1085
01:01:34,813 --> 01:01:35,771
What help?

1086
01:01:35,845 --> 01:01:37,738
Let's go to the police.

1087
01:01:37,763 --> 01:01:39,721
No police. No police.

1088
01:01:39,896 --> 01:01:42,266
You believed me because I'm your friend.

1089
01:01:42,291 --> 01:01:45,542
If they don't believe me,
I'll become a murderer.

1090
01:01:45,969 --> 01:01:47,761
The whole family will be humiliated.

1091
01:01:48,035 --> 01:01:50,796
Especially with the wedding coming up.

1092
01:01:50,821 --> 01:01:54,657
I don't mind helping
with rangolis and cooking.

1093
01:01:54,848 --> 01:01:56,351
But a dead body!

1094
01:01:59,048 --> 01:02:00,257
I knew it.

1095
01:02:01,470 --> 01:02:05,678
My life has been tough since childhood.

1096
01:02:05,861 --> 01:02:07,194
Shut up! Just shut up!

1097
01:02:07,292 --> 01:02:08,367
Tell me what to do.

1098
01:02:10,719 --> 01:02:11,886
Tell me what to do.

1099
01:02:13,495 --> 01:02:15,406
[water splatters]

1100
01:02:18,671 --> 01:02:19,546
Grab the rope.

1101
01:02:22,226 --> 01:02:23,184
Place your finger.

1102
01:02:23,491 --> 01:02:24,335
Where?

1103
01:02:27,941 --> 01:02:29,941
[eerie music playing]

1104
01:02:31,714 --> 01:02:33,841
Hold the feet. That side is lighter.

1105
01:02:34,015 --> 01:02:37,684
You can't tell between
types of dal but you know this!

1106
01:02:38,217 --> 01:02:39,050
Pick it up.

1107
01:02:39,407 --> 01:02:40,824
Slowly, slowly.

1108
01:02:43,751 --> 01:02:46,580
[grandma murmuring chants]

1109
01:02:47,944 --> 01:02:48,937
Oh, lord! Help us.

1110
01:02:48,962 --> 01:02:49,962
Statue.

1111
01:02:59,396 --> 01:03:00,576
Let's go. Let's go.

1112
01:03:01,972 --> 01:03:03,972
[footsteps thudding]

1113
01:03:10,398 --> 01:03:12,398
[heavy breathing]

1114
01:03:32,499 --> 01:03:35,302
Don't tell me you're going
to kill grandma as well.

1115
01:03:35,330 --> 01:03:36,293
Shut up!

1116
01:03:36,404 --> 01:03:37,819
[glass clinks]

1117
01:03:38,707 --> 01:03:40,761
Bloody cat! No sense of time!

1118
01:03:45,742 --> 01:03:47,001
[door creaks]

1119
01:03:51,500 --> 01:03:53,917
Kiranmayi, we'll go that way.

1120
01:03:54,371 --> 01:03:56,329
I can't do it.

1121
01:03:56,564 --> 01:03:59,273
-Just 5 more steps.
-No way!

1122
01:03:59,716 --> 01:04:01,258
It's easily 500 steps.

1123
01:04:01,742 --> 01:04:04,717
Kiranmayi, let's come on!

1124
01:04:05,766 --> 01:04:06,775
Let's come on!

1125
01:04:06,800 --> 01:04:08,800
[dramatic music playing]

1126
01:04:10,131 --> 01:04:11,553
[panting]

1127
01:04:30,536 --> 01:04:31,703
I'm done!

1128
01:04:32,392 --> 01:04:33,559
You go ahead.

1129
01:04:38,185 --> 01:04:40,250
Never mind. You can't lift it alone.

1130
01:04:41,519 --> 01:04:42,494
Close the door.

1131
01:04:52,851 --> 01:04:53,899
-Push the car.
-Huh?

1132
01:04:53,924 --> 01:04:57,150
The engine sound will wake
people up. Now push it!

1133
01:05:09,733 --> 01:05:11,577
[car engine revs]

1134
01:05:19,516 --> 01:05:21,115
[tires screeching ]

1135
01:05:22,795 --> 01:05:24,047
[door clunks]

1136
01:05:24,092 --> 01:05:25,202
[thud]

1137
01:05:25,227 --> 01:05:26,995
[water splatters]

1138
01:05:27,770 --> 01:05:28,992
[sighs]

1139
01:05:33,666 --> 01:05:35,666
[car engine revs]

1140
01:05:56,824 --> 01:05:58,824
[melancholic music playing]

1141
01:06:17,704 --> 01:06:19,110
What happened here?

1142
01:06:19,134 --> 01:06:22,646
I used to make so many desserts with this.

1143
01:06:23,361 --> 01:06:24,933
Do you think it shrunk because of heat?

1144
01:06:25,004 --> 01:06:27,098
No. It looks more like...

1145
01:06:28,331 --> 01:06:30,150
someone's head has been...

1146
01:06:30,188 --> 01:06:30,944
[thud]

1147
01:06:30,968 --> 01:06:32,339
whacked with it.

1148
01:06:32,984 --> 01:06:34,783
I mean, for it to bend like this,

1149
01:06:34,807 --> 01:06:37,351
someone like me must have hit it hard.

1150
01:06:37,391 --> 01:06:38,657
Who else could it be?

1151
01:06:39,637 --> 01:06:41,939
-Where did you find this?
-On the front porch.

1152
01:06:43,926 --> 01:06:45,833
How did it end up there?

1153
01:06:46,909 --> 01:06:48,628
Yeah, I wonder.

1154
01:06:55,741 --> 01:06:58,937
I must be so dumb if it took
me this long to figure it out.

1155
01:06:59,894 --> 01:07:02,254
My mind was so foggy after
what happened yesterday.

1156
01:07:04,793 --> 01:07:05,881
But I'm ready for it now.

1157
01:07:06,391 --> 01:07:07,474
Who are you?

1158
01:07:08,797 --> 01:07:09,811
I'm sorry.

1159
01:07:11,071 --> 01:07:13,025
I didn't mean to drag you into this.

1160
01:07:16,968 --> 01:07:18,832
Where do I begin?

1161
01:07:19,656 --> 01:07:22,969
Life was good when we lived
together at the orphanage.

1162
01:07:23,270 --> 01:07:26,418
We were inseparable.

1163
01:07:29,477 --> 01:07:31,688
Do you remember the hostel warden?

1164
01:07:31,888 --> 01:07:33,294
That monster?

1165
01:07:38,988 --> 01:07:41,773
I was happy that you
found a nice family...

1166
01:07:42,243 --> 01:07:44,611
and got out of that misery.

1167
01:07:47,779 --> 01:07:49,437
But once you left,

1168
01:07:49,849 --> 01:07:51,666
I became his target.

1169
01:07:56,431 --> 01:07:59,164
I couldn't stay there
anymore and so, I ran away.

1170
01:07:59,591 --> 01:08:01,064
I didn't know where to go.

1171
01:08:01,221 --> 01:08:02,301
But I had to get out of there.

1172
01:08:02,368 --> 01:08:05,446
Maybe this journey was
meant to strengthen me.

1173
01:08:05,937 --> 01:08:07,116
I sought shelter at various places.

1174
01:08:08,019 --> 01:08:09,968
I did every job I could find.

1175
01:08:10,217 --> 01:08:12,546
No one showed me any kindness.

1176
01:08:12,624 --> 01:08:15,918
I pursued distant education while
I was working at this one place.

1177
01:08:16,181 --> 01:08:18,515
But there was this
scoundrel over there as well.

1178
01:08:18,805 --> 01:08:19,604
Swarna...

1179
01:08:20,152 --> 01:08:22,160
He would try really hard to exploit me.

1180
01:08:22,185 --> 01:08:22,925
Swarna...

1181
01:08:23,627 --> 01:08:25,703
I would be shivering with fear all night.

1182
01:08:25,960 --> 01:08:26,798
But then...

1183
01:08:26,822 --> 01:08:30,570
there's only so many times
or places I can run away to.

1184
01:08:31,071 --> 01:08:33,812
One night, a bunch of people showed up.

1185
01:08:33,993 --> 01:08:35,709
You guys go carefully.
We'll be here for 4 days.

1186
01:08:35,734 --> 01:08:38,264
They were hiding from the police.

1187
01:08:38,563 --> 01:08:39,978
They stayed for a couple of days.

1188
01:08:44,360 --> 01:08:46,484
I couldn't tell if they were
good people or bad people.

1189
01:08:46,622 --> 01:08:47,812
They were fearless, for sure.

1190
01:08:48,063 --> 01:08:49,762
That was the first time...

1191
01:08:49,828 --> 01:08:51,277
I saw how fearless people looked.

1192
01:08:52,198 --> 01:08:54,224
I thought I was getting a read on them.

1193
01:08:54,435 --> 01:08:58,053
Little did I know that one of them
was watching me very closely.

1194
01:09:00,326 --> 01:09:05,163
Remember. We're doing it
for those who face injustice.

1195
01:09:05,188 --> 01:09:08,043
You can achieve your
goal only if you let go of fear.

1196
01:09:08,068 --> 01:09:11,222
It felt like he was
directly talking to me.

1197
01:09:11,369 --> 01:09:15,996
I decided to overcome
my fear and fight back.

1198
01:09:18,599 --> 01:09:20,599
[intense music sets in]

1199
01:09:21,376 --> 01:09:23,512
[door creaks]

1200
01:09:34,111 --> 01:09:35,229
[door creaks]

1201
01:09:37,048 --> 01:09:38,039
Oh!

1202
01:09:38,894 --> 01:09:40,532
You left the door open for me.

1203
01:09:40,990 --> 01:09:43,006
You finally got my hints?

1204
01:09:43,208 --> 01:09:43,969
[gasps]

1205
01:09:43,993 --> 01:09:45,106
No, don't!

1206
01:09:46,075 --> 01:09:47,426
[knife whooshes]

1207
01:09:47,450 --> 01:09:48,963
[screams]

1208
01:09:52,870 --> 01:09:54,751
[groans]

1209
01:09:57,151 --> 01:09:58,870
[shrill cry]

1210
01:09:58,945 --> 01:10:01,292
If 5 people mourn his death,

1211
01:10:01,316 --> 01:10:03,018
there are 30 who celebrate it.

1212
01:10:03,089 --> 01:10:05,527
Remember this math, always.

1213
01:10:05,552 --> 01:10:06,989
If the math makes sense to you,

1214
01:10:07,014 --> 01:10:09,723
forget about grief, and whether
it's something wrong to do.

1215
01:10:13,305 --> 01:10:14,349
Will you join us?

1216
01:10:14,886 --> 01:10:18,183
I spent my whole life being
aimless and directionless.

1217
01:10:18,409 --> 01:10:20,035
When they asked me to join them,

1218
01:10:20,157 --> 01:10:22,994
I didn't think if it was right or wrong.

1219
01:10:23,198 --> 01:10:24,727
I left with them.

1220
01:10:25,652 --> 01:10:28,445
My life had completely changed.

1221
01:10:30,236 --> 01:10:31,703
Including my name.

1222
01:10:31,789 --> 01:10:32,685
Jhansi.

1223
01:10:33,347 --> 01:10:34,329
That's your name from today.

1224
01:10:37,080 --> 01:10:38,617
[bikes revving]

1225
01:10:40,097 --> 01:10:43,613
It doesn't matter if our
target is rich or powerful.

1226
01:10:43,737 --> 01:10:46,394
If he has wronged, I
will make him pay for it.

1227
01:10:47,213 --> 01:10:48,409
They're from the neighboring village.

1228
01:10:48,434 --> 01:10:49,222
Jhansi...

1229
01:10:50,971 --> 01:10:53,067
[intense music playing]

1230
01:11:03,817 --> 01:11:07,073
When you spend all
your life feeling unloved,

1231
01:11:07,239 --> 01:11:10,555
you settle for bare
minimum and call it love.

1232
01:11:17,667 --> 01:11:19,781
You're really special, Jhansi.

1233
01:11:19,806 --> 01:11:21,296
I'm glad I found you.

1234
01:11:21,342 --> 01:11:23,689
I'll train you like a warrior.

1235
01:11:24,461 --> 01:11:25,771
[gun clicks]

1236
01:11:28,509 --> 01:11:29,813
[music intensifies]

1237
01:11:29,843 --> 01:11:31,153
[gun clicks]

1238
01:11:32,325 --> 01:11:33,702
[gun shot fired]

1239
01:11:34,013 --> 01:11:35,226
[thud]

1240
01:11:39,345 --> 01:11:41,019
[revolver clicks]

1241
01:11:41,034 --> 01:11:43,537
[exploding]

1242
01:11:44,465 --> 01:11:46,053
It didn't occur to me back then...

1243
01:11:46,897 --> 01:11:49,808
that he's a wolf hiding behind
the mask of a good man.

1244
01:11:53,515 --> 01:11:55,662
He hand picked me with the intention of...

1245
01:11:55,966 --> 01:11:58,394
moulding me as per his agenda.

1246
01:11:58,896 --> 01:12:02,728
We all came together for
the common good, until...

1247
01:12:02,753 --> 01:12:04,210
Karuna, who are they?

1248
01:12:06,957 --> 01:12:08,357
You sold your soul, Karuna.

1249
01:12:08,958 --> 01:12:13,156
But he used us for his selfish purposes.

1250
01:12:18,275 --> 01:12:22,635
One day, while the
police were chasing us...

1251
01:12:23,655 --> 01:12:26,136
You're safe only as long as you obey him.

1252
01:12:26,253 --> 01:12:27,636
Once you go against him,

1253
01:12:27,706 --> 01:12:30,337
he will get his revenge
when the time is right.

1254
01:12:30,362 --> 01:12:31,424
Jhansi, run!

1255
01:12:31,565 --> 01:12:32,820
[gun shots firing]

1256
01:12:32,844 --> 01:12:33,980
[grunts]

1257
01:12:36,799 --> 01:12:38,773
Leave him! Run, run!

1258
01:12:39,213 --> 01:12:40,829
Karuna, please help!

1259
01:12:41,198 --> 01:12:42,047
Karuna!

1260
01:12:42,072 --> 01:12:42,988
Karuna, please!

1261
01:12:43,032 --> 01:12:43,881
Karuna!

1262
01:12:43,906 --> 01:12:46,179
[gun shots continue firing]

1263
01:12:46,934 --> 01:12:48,242
Shiva wasn't spared either,

1264
01:12:48,510 --> 01:12:50,945
even though he was like a brother to him.

1265
01:12:52,387 --> 01:12:53,818
He's dead because of you.

1266
01:12:53,843 --> 01:12:56,085
He came back because he fancied you,

1267
01:12:56,109 --> 01:12:57,184
and got himself killed.

1268
01:12:57,209 --> 01:12:59,832
He blamed me for his mistake.

1269
01:12:59,980 --> 01:13:01,906
I didn't get his intentions back then.

1270
01:13:01,951 --> 01:13:03,247
[crying]

1271
01:13:05,582 --> 01:13:09,006
I was shattered that Shiva
was dead because of me.

1272
01:13:09,526 --> 01:13:12,863
Fear slowly started creeping back in.

1273
01:13:15,089 --> 01:13:18,033
I brought your favorite
idli karam podi. Have it.

1274
01:13:19,670 --> 01:13:22,292
Whatever I say is for your own good.

1275
01:13:22,715 --> 01:13:24,986
You'll see it someday.

1276
01:13:25,405 --> 01:13:30,776
Men like him suppress you
and turn you into puppets,

1277
01:13:30,801 --> 01:13:34,163
while pretending to be
innocent, loving men.

1278
01:13:34,397 --> 01:13:35,623
But the truth is,

1279
01:13:35,648 --> 01:13:38,388
he's been looking for someone like me.

1280
01:13:38,587 --> 01:13:40,358
Someone who has lost everything in life.

1281
01:13:41,270 --> 01:13:43,245
I decided that night...

1282
01:13:43,564 --> 01:13:46,684
to break free from there.

1283
01:13:47,069 --> 01:13:50,856
But he sensed it somehow,
and kept watching me closely.

1284
01:13:51,347 --> 01:13:53,584
He built these walls around me...

1285
01:13:53,844 --> 01:13:55,937
and controlled my movements 24X7.

1286
01:13:57,739 --> 01:14:00,762
I couldn't do anything
but watch his atrocities.

1287
01:14:04,815 --> 01:14:06,549
[gun shots fired]

1288
01:14:27,362 --> 01:14:30,115
I was slowly dying inside.

1289
01:14:33,673 --> 01:14:36,948
That's when I decided
to get him arrested...

1290
01:14:37,283 --> 01:14:39,340
even if it meant losing my life.

1291
01:14:53,548 --> 01:14:55,651
[intense music playing]

1292
01:15:00,697 --> 01:15:04,510
He thought he saved
all of us from the police.

1293
01:15:08,499 --> 01:15:10,199
The fact that I trusted...

1294
01:15:10,691 --> 01:15:12,574
such a monster blindly...

1295
01:15:13,050 --> 01:15:14,663
makes me so angry...

1296
01:15:16,079 --> 01:15:16,954
and disgusted by myself.

1297
01:15:18,884 --> 01:15:21,747
He committed so many
atrocities right in front of my eyes.

1298
01:15:23,028 --> 01:15:24,304
I just stood there, watching.

1299
01:15:26,403 --> 01:15:27,676
Was it out of fear?

1300
01:15:28,614 --> 01:15:29,824
Or something else?

1301
01:15:33,283 --> 01:15:34,215
I just know that...

1302
01:15:34,960 --> 01:15:36,360
I felt hopeless.

1303
01:15:40,640 --> 01:15:43,688
It took me a lot of time
to recover from that.

1304
01:15:44,631 --> 01:15:45,880
I can neither forget...

1305
01:15:46,512 --> 01:15:47,777
nor forgive myself.

1306
01:15:51,937 --> 01:15:55,721
So I thought it was best to
erase those memories from my life.

1307
01:15:56,860 --> 01:16:00,304
I never told anyone about these things.

1308
01:16:00,833 --> 01:16:01,673
Not you.

1309
01:16:02,742 --> 01:16:03,821
Not Ani.

1310
01:16:06,332 --> 01:16:07,460
The fact that you survived all this...

1311
01:16:07,485 --> 01:16:09,535
and restarted your life is unbelievable!

1312
01:16:11,367 --> 01:16:13,370
I wouldn't have been able to do it.

1313
01:16:13,559 --> 01:16:16,068
I'm sorry I couldn't help you, Swarna.

1314
01:16:16,653 --> 01:16:21,156
Now some guy is stalking
me and trying to attack me.

1315
01:16:21,417 --> 01:16:25,178
I have a feeling Karuna is behind this.

1316
01:16:29,022 --> 01:16:29,842
Brother...

1317
01:16:30,050 --> 01:16:31,224
Venkanna is dead.

1318
01:16:32,899 --> 01:16:34,939
I guess I finally found Jhansi.

1319
01:16:34,951 --> 01:16:36,951
[intense music builds up]

1320
01:16:37,458 --> 01:16:41,289
If he gets to know where I am,

1321
01:16:41,903 --> 01:16:44,278
he'll go to any lengths to come find me.

1322
01:16:44,315 --> 01:16:46,048
[steam hissing]

1323
01:16:55,418 --> 01:16:56,788
[knife whooshes]

1324
01:17:07,665 --> 01:17:10,137
Oh, lord! Someone stabbed Srinu!

1325
01:17:10,162 --> 01:17:12,835
He's bleeding heavily. Guys, help!

1326
01:17:13,879 --> 01:17:15,879
[intense music continues]

1327
01:17:19,495 --> 01:17:21,243
[gas hissing]

1328
01:17:21,324 --> 01:17:22,620
[metal clanks]

1329
01:17:22,843 --> 01:17:24,554
[matchstick strikes]

1330
01:17:24,821 --> 01:17:26,963
[explosion]

1331
01:18:00,305 --> 01:18:01,431
Who is this?

1332
01:18:01,824 --> 01:18:03,991
-She's my childhood friend.
-Friend?

1333
01:18:04,253 --> 01:18:05,919
Did you come with all your stuff?

1334
01:18:08,471 --> 01:18:11,180
My husband and I got into a huge fight.

1335
01:18:12,353 --> 01:18:14,102
He yelled, I yelled back.

1336
01:18:14,171 --> 01:18:15,421
He yelled loudly,

1337
01:18:15,446 --> 01:18:17,790
I yelled back a little less loudly.

1338
01:18:18,129 --> 01:18:19,980
He was coming towards
me with his hand raised.

1339
01:18:20,004 --> 01:18:22,504
I panicked and hit him
before he could hit me.

1340
01:18:24,041 --> 01:18:26,291
I realized later that he
wasn't coming to hit me.

1341
01:18:26,316 --> 01:18:28,979
He was just trying to
turn on the fan switch.

1342
01:18:29,498 --> 01:18:33,207
I left the house because I
was worried that he would.

1343
01:18:33,380 --> 01:18:34,254
It's alright.

1344
01:18:34,380 --> 01:18:36,671
If he ever decides
to hit you in the future,

1345
01:18:36,696 --> 01:18:38,279
he will think twice.

1346
01:18:39,577 --> 01:18:41,345
So, what did you and
your husband fight about?

1347
01:18:41,629 --> 01:18:43,339
Hey, don't get personal.

1348
01:18:43,730 --> 01:18:46,129
You can stay here as long as you'd like.

1349
01:18:46,171 --> 01:18:47,338
Feel at home.

1350
01:18:47,587 --> 01:18:50,504
You're Swarna's friend,
and that makes you family.

1351
01:18:51,088 --> 01:18:52,526
Take her inside, Swarna.

1352
01:18:54,558 --> 01:18:56,754
So, this is your cooking
and rangoli set-up.

1353
01:18:57,062 --> 01:18:59,104
Don't say set-up. It sounds wrong.

1354
01:18:59,129 --> 01:19:00,791
You two are unbelievable!

1355
01:19:01,727 --> 01:19:06,218
Sister-in-law, I figured a
secret about your cooking.

1356
01:19:07,337 --> 01:19:09,930
You taught her how to cook, didn't you?

1357
01:19:15,092 --> 01:19:17,134
You taught me to cook, huh?

1358
01:19:17,765 --> 01:19:19,879
You can't resist cooking, can you?

1359
01:19:20,227 --> 01:19:22,314
You have to show off your talent.

1360
01:19:22,504 --> 01:19:25,294
If you can't resist,
just add salt in the end.

1361
01:19:25,339 --> 01:19:28,255
But don't get excited and cook like me.

1362
01:19:28,280 --> 01:19:30,257
Cook like you? Are you serious?

1363
01:19:30,282 --> 01:19:33,792
Hey! Your friend's
fish curry is delicious!

1364
01:19:33,817 --> 01:19:36,047
-I only taught her.
-Really?

1365
01:19:36,351 --> 01:19:38,309
Okay. Let me see what else she made.

1366
01:19:50,097 --> 01:19:53,873
"Our little girl with the
twin braids is a bride now"

1367
01:19:53,940 --> 01:19:57,769
"Yet you're still the same as ever"

1368
01:19:57,802 --> 01:20:01,495
"Everyone knows that
stubborn streak of yours"

1369
01:20:01,519 --> 01:20:05,412
"You still charge through
life without a care"

1370
01:20:05,436 --> 01:20:09,203
"We've been hearing
the whispers everywhere"

1371
01:20:09,227 --> 01:20:13,162
"Tell us, how did you manage
to get the man you wanted?"

1372
01:20:20,631 --> 01:20:24,642
"How long are you going to
sit there all shy and quiet?"

1373
01:20:24,667 --> 01:20:28,391
"Come on, sweetheart"

1374
01:20:28,820 --> 01:20:32,653
"Why wait? Let's show them who we are"

1375
01:20:32,677 --> 01:20:35,552
"Walking in like queens"

1376
01:20:35,576 --> 01:20:39,463
"Bride, what's the rush?"

1377
01:20:39,490 --> 01:20:42,604
"The best part is yet to come"

1378
01:20:42,647 --> 01:20:46,456
"Attagirl! We're not holding back"

1379
01:20:46,480 --> 01:20:50,331
"A girl should have a little spirit"

1380
01:20:50,355 --> 01:20:54,164
"Attagirl! Let the smiles spill over"

1381
01:20:54,188 --> 01:20:58,209
"This is our celebration
Who's going to stop us?"

1382
01:20:58,234 --> 01:21:02,932
"Have the time of your life"

1383
01:21:06,795 --> 01:21:10,490
"Let's see what marriage does to you"

1384
01:21:10,514 --> 01:21:14,331
"Though I doubt it'll tame your mischief"

1385
01:21:14,355 --> 01:21:17,709
"Don't worry, I'll transform
my mother-in-law"

1386
01:21:17,736 --> 01:21:21,059
"Into an older version of me"

1387
01:21:21,083 --> 01:21:26,072
"Alright girls, enough of the commotion"

1388
01:21:26,096 --> 01:21:29,723
"The auspicious time is slipping away"

1389
01:21:29,748 --> 01:21:33,769
"That's enough of your playful antics"

1390
01:21:33,793 --> 01:21:37,421
"These tricks won't fly
at your in-laws' house"

1391
01:21:37,446 --> 01:21:44,020
"Oh, come on! I'm still
the Queen of my house!"

1392
01:21:44,038 --> 01:21:47,847
"Attagirl! We're not holding back"

1393
01:21:47,871 --> 01:21:51,722
"A girl should have a little spirit"

1394
01:21:51,746 --> 01:21:55,555
"Attagirl! Let the smiles spill over"

1395
01:21:55,579 --> 01:21:59,624
"This is our celebration
Who's going to stop us?"

1396
01:21:59,649 --> 01:22:04,347
"Have the time of your life"

1397
01:22:11,933 --> 01:22:19,414
"In this garden of happiness,
as I come into bloom"

1398
01:22:19,490 --> 01:22:27,490
"Is my past going to
float around off shore?"

1399
01:22:34,719 --> 01:22:41,705
"Oh, come on! You're still
the Queen of our house!"

1400
