Don't you see my blood
burning with rebellion?

1428
01:24:52,930 --> 01:24:56,061
Don't you hear the roaring of my heart?

1429
01:24:59,089 --> 01:25:00,458
[thud]

1430
01:25:03,538 --> 01:25:05,959
[thud sounds continue]

1431
01:25:16,801 --> 01:25:18,071
Did Karuna send you?

1432
01:25:18,341 --> 01:25:18,974
Yes.

1433
01:25:18,999 --> 01:25:20,676
I would've showed up if he called.

1434
01:25:22,311 --> 01:25:23,252
Where is he now?

1435
01:25:23,277 --> 01:25:24,250
At the river bank.

1436
01:25:24,577 --> 01:25:26,577
[gun clanks]

1437
01:25:28,436 --> 01:25:30,116
[eerie music playing]

1438
01:25:40,482 --> 01:25:41,356
Out!

1439
01:25:42,341 --> 01:25:45,910
I told you she'd hear my
voice and come running.

1440
01:25:52,128 --> 01:25:54,083
[eagle shrieking]

1441
01:25:59,087 --> 01:26:01,421
You look ravishing!

1442
01:26:03,347 --> 01:26:04,930
You haven't changed a bit.

1443
01:26:07,187 --> 01:26:09,521
I have trained you well.

1444
01:26:11,998 --> 01:26:12,956
Come close.

1445
01:26:13,706 --> 01:26:14,373
Come.

1446
01:26:20,887 --> 01:26:22,845
It's been so many years, Jhansi.

1447
01:26:37,388 --> 01:26:38,595
[sighs]

1448
01:26:39,239 --> 01:26:40,530
I don't go by that name anymore.

1449
01:26:43,072 --> 01:26:45,697
Everyone here calls me Swarna.

1450
01:26:45,738 --> 01:26:46,839
Who do you mean by everyone?

1451
01:26:48,363 --> 01:26:50,738
-My family.
-Family?

1452
01:26:51,364 --> 01:26:52,447
Who all are there?

1453
01:26:54,197 --> 01:26:55,530
I got married, Karuna.

1454
01:26:55,947 --> 01:26:57,030
Holy crap!

1455
01:26:58,445 --> 01:26:59,986
You got married?

1456
01:27:00,613 --> 01:27:04,613
The one thing I was dreading
to hear, and here goes.

1457
01:27:05,320 --> 01:27:07,194
[shrieking in frustration]

1458
01:27:13,603 --> 01:27:14,895
Are you really married?

1459
01:27:16,072 --> 01:27:16,947
Really?

1460
01:27:17,239 --> 01:27:18,530
I gave you this life.

1461
01:27:18,555 --> 01:27:20,097
I taught you everything you know.

1462
01:27:20,613 --> 01:27:23,322
I made sure the cops didn't get to you.

1463
01:27:23,613 --> 01:27:25,919
But someone tipped them about me.

1464
01:27:27,344 --> 01:27:29,177
You were on my mind all day...

1465
01:27:29,202 --> 01:27:31,119
even when I was in jail.

1466
01:27:31,460 --> 01:27:33,877
I wanted to marry you once I got out.

1467
01:27:34,678 --> 01:27:37,011
I never confessed my
love but, you knew, right?

1468
01:27:38,761 --> 01:27:42,011
I thought you'd take one look
at me and come running.

1469
01:27:42,970 --> 01:27:44,219
But now...

1470
01:27:46,994 --> 01:27:49,285
I don't know why you're here, Karuna.

1471
01:27:50,555 --> 01:27:53,138
Do I have to spell it out for you?

1472
01:27:59,154 --> 01:28:00,154
Karuna, listen.

1473
01:28:02,058 --> 01:28:03,308
It's thanks to you...

1474
01:28:04,553 --> 01:28:06,358
that I could turn over a new leaf.

1475
01:28:07,844 --> 01:28:08,928
Let things...

1476
01:28:09,601 --> 01:28:10,810
stay as they are.

1477
01:28:12,552 --> 01:28:13,511
New life, huh?

1478
01:28:15,011 --> 01:28:15,928
You're right.

1479
01:28:17,511 --> 01:28:20,216
I'm sure you told your
family about your old life.

1480
01:28:22,261 --> 01:28:23,386
You did, right?

1481
01:28:26,052 --> 01:28:28,094
Oh, you didn't?

1482
01:28:29,973 --> 01:28:31,664
You must have told your husband at least.

1483
01:28:34,177 --> 01:28:35,469
Jhansi, are you serious?

1484
01:28:35,624 --> 01:28:37,332
Not even your husband knows?

1485
01:28:38,484 --> 01:28:39,605
You poor thing.

1486
01:28:41,177 --> 01:28:42,177
Don't panic.

1487
01:28:42,678 --> 01:28:43,636
I won't tell him.

1488
01:28:44,545 --> 01:28:45,461
Karuna...

1489
01:28:48,233 --> 01:28:49,161
Leave me alone.

1490
01:28:49,761 --> 01:28:51,177
I have a family now.

1491
01:28:51,202 --> 01:28:53,619
Why are you begging me so desperately?

1492
01:28:54,209 --> 01:28:55,987
I can't see you like this.

1493
01:28:56,030 --> 01:28:58,422
Karuna... Karuna, please.

1494
01:28:58,510 --> 01:28:59,594
Leave me alone.

1495
01:28:59,731 --> 01:29:01,275
Alright, stop begging.

1496
01:29:01,299 --> 01:29:03,029
I can't see you like this. I will leave.

1497
01:29:03,919 --> 01:29:05,210
You be happy.

1498
01:29:05,545 --> 01:29:06,295
Go.

1499
01:29:12,365 --> 01:29:13,365
Can I trust you?

1500
01:29:14,353 --> 01:29:18,020
-You will leave, right?
-I promise.

1501
01:29:18,517 --> 01:29:19,392
Satisfied?

1502
01:29:22,450 --> 01:29:24,450
[eerie music sets in]

1503
01:29:31,973 --> 01:29:34,556
God forbid something
happens to your family...

1504
01:29:36,602 --> 01:29:38,102
I pray that it doesn't.

1505
01:29:38,391 --> 01:29:39,933
But God forbid!

1506
01:29:40,348 --> 01:29:42,848
Who's going to save them?
Swarna or Jhansi?

1507
01:29:46,499 --> 01:29:47,582
Go, go.

1508
01:29:48,089 --> 01:29:50,881
Your family must be looking for you.

1509
01:29:57,218 --> 01:29:59,218
[intense music playing]

1510
01:30:11,227 --> 01:30:12,465
When are we going back home?

1511
01:30:12,489 --> 01:30:14,104
We decided to stay
till the wedding, right?

1512
01:30:14,128 --> 01:30:15,128
Of course.

1513
01:30:15,872 --> 01:30:17,174
The wedding.

1514
01:30:19,776 --> 01:30:20,818
What's wrong, Swarna?

1515
01:30:21,083 --> 01:30:22,250
Why do you look so worried?

1516
01:30:23,320 --> 01:30:24,587
Did someone say something?

1517
01:30:24,951 --> 01:30:26,132
We'll talk about it later.

1518
01:30:27,480 --> 01:30:28,677
You don't have to hesitate with me.

1519
01:30:28,857 --> 01:30:30,440
Tell me what's bothering you.

1520
01:30:35,542 --> 01:30:36,913
There's a lot to tell you, Ani.

1521
01:30:38,047 --> 01:30:39,548
Yes, I came here to tell you.

1522
01:30:41,203 --> 01:30:42,411
But now's not the time.

1523
01:30:43,204 --> 01:30:44,788
I'll wait until after the wedding.

1524
01:30:46,997 --> 01:30:48,288
I'll tell you everything.

1525
01:30:53,631 --> 01:30:54,459
Alright.

1526
01:30:54,498 --> 01:30:55,579
[crickets chirping]

1527
01:30:55,603 --> 01:30:56,652
Family!

1528
01:30:58,026 --> 01:31:00,068
What the hell does that mean?

1529
01:31:00,866 --> 01:31:02,885
Aren't I her family?

1530
01:31:03,157 --> 01:31:05,307
Then why did you send
her away with good wishes?

1531
01:31:05,960 --> 01:31:06,802
I know.

1532
01:31:07,153 --> 01:31:08,990
I know I spoke like an idiot.

1533
01:31:10,121 --> 01:31:11,923
But I'm not.

1534
01:31:11,948 --> 01:31:13,856
Why would I let her go?

1535
01:31:14,973 --> 01:31:16,397
She is mine.

1536
01:31:17,536 --> 01:31:18,505
Mine!

1537
01:31:22,034 --> 01:31:26,194
Let me have a little fun with her.

1538
01:31:30,115 --> 01:31:32,739
Who is her husband, what does he do,

1539
01:31:32,764 --> 01:31:36,014
who all are in the family, and
what are their weaknesses.

1540
01:31:36,626 --> 01:31:39,381
Get me all the information
before I get sober.

1541
01:31:42,514 --> 01:31:45,634
[on tape recorder] Don't you see
my blood burning with rebellion?

1542
01:31:46,438 --> 01:31:49,356
Don't you hear the roaring of my heart?

1543
01:31:49,512 --> 01:31:51,490
This is the song that I heard, sir.

1544
01:31:51,971 --> 01:31:52,836
[button clicks]

1545
01:31:52,860 --> 01:31:55,742
8 years ago, when I was
posted in Ananthapur,

1546
01:31:56,055 --> 01:31:58,355
they played the same song
all over the village back then.

1547
01:31:58,380 --> 01:32:01,839
Within the next few days,
the local MLA was shot dead.

1548
01:32:02,160 --> 01:32:05,494
Probably, they're using
this song as a warning.

1549
01:32:05,511 --> 01:32:07,493
[alarming music playing]

1550
01:32:07,517 --> 01:32:09,298
Who are they warning now, sir?

1551
01:32:09,959 --> 01:32:12,543
The CM meeting is in 2 days.

1552
01:32:12,978 --> 01:32:16,770
Call the Commissioner's Office
and get all the gang details.

1553
01:32:18,248 --> 01:32:19,207
Yes, sir.

1554
01:32:20,768 --> 01:32:22,751
CM has approved your nomination.

1555
01:32:22,822 --> 01:32:24,989
He is going to be present
for the campaigning.

1556
01:32:25,070 --> 01:32:29,737
I think it's advisable to give
the party ticket to someone else.

1557
01:32:30,355 --> 01:32:33,146
Even my health isn't
keeping up these days.

1558
01:32:34,397 --> 01:32:36,230
So, what are you proposing we do now?

1559
01:32:36,428 --> 01:32:39,886
There are far more experienced
candidates in the party.

1560
01:32:39,990 --> 01:32:42,073
You mean Madhusudhan Rao?

1561
01:32:44,666 --> 01:32:45,666
Got it.

1562
01:32:45,927 --> 01:32:47,094
You may leave.

1563
01:32:48,199 --> 01:32:49,821
Please forgive me.

1564
01:32:51,294 --> 01:32:53,752
Looks like Madhusudhan
is back to his old groove.

1565
01:32:54,653 --> 01:32:56,894
He's crossing the line
and testing my patience.

1566
01:32:57,333 --> 01:32:59,134
Let's show him what we can do.

1567
01:32:59,434 --> 01:33:02,309
Pull all the files on the liquor scam.

1568
01:33:03,108 --> 01:33:03,899
Let's go.

1569
01:33:05,756 --> 01:33:07,674
[bikes rev]

1570
01:33:18,299 --> 01:33:20,299
[suspenseful music playing]

1571
01:33:27,502 --> 01:33:31,177
How dare he expose my liquor scam files!

1572
01:33:31,202 --> 01:33:32,616
Ramaiah Raju ain't a saint, is he?

1573
01:33:32,985 --> 01:33:36,339
He's so jealous of my popularity
in public, he resents me.

1574
01:33:36,466 --> 01:33:37,757
Who doesn't have a dirty past?

1575
01:33:37,918 --> 01:33:39,001
I'm sure he does too.

1576
01:33:39,134 --> 01:33:40,592
I'll go digging too.

1577
01:33:40,985 --> 01:33:42,152
I will give him a taste of...

1578
01:33:42,853 --> 01:33:43,966
Who is he?

1579
01:33:45,633 --> 01:33:46,675
Who the hell are you?

1580
01:33:47,654 --> 01:33:48,654
Let me speak.

1581
01:33:49,341 --> 01:33:50,299
It's a business deal.

1582
01:33:52,474 --> 01:33:55,224
People like us have a
history of erasing lives.

1583
01:33:55,249 --> 01:33:56,624
And that comes with fear.

1584
01:33:58,043 --> 01:34:02,168
When we give some of this fear
back to them, they start fearing us.

1585
01:34:02,193 --> 01:34:03,984
-We control them.
-Hey!

1586
01:34:04,314 --> 01:34:05,230
What the hell are you talking about?

1587
01:34:05,659 --> 01:34:09,284
Ramaiah Raju is going to submit
your files to the CM tomorrow morning.

1588
01:34:10,610 --> 01:34:11,777
Liquor scam.

1589
01:34:12,803 --> 01:34:14,483
The files only talk about 10 crores.

1590
01:34:14,804 --> 01:34:18,165
If they dig deeper, they will
get to the remaining 20 crores.

1591
01:34:18,286 --> 01:34:21,911
Further digging, and the murder
you committed for it will also be out.

1592
01:34:23,170 --> 01:34:25,651
You guys step outside. Go.

1593
01:34:27,872 --> 01:34:29,872
See all those men?

1594
01:34:30,127 --> 01:34:33,564
What are you going to
do differently that we can't?

1595
01:34:34,776 --> 01:34:38,359
There was an Inspector called
Sridhar Naidu in your constituency.

1596
01:34:39,120 --> 01:34:40,222
Remember him?

1597
01:34:40,277 --> 01:34:42,611
He suffered sudden death one day.

1598
01:34:42,713 --> 01:34:45,671
The Paderu Bridge also
happened to collapse the same day.

1599
01:34:45,943 --> 01:34:47,402
It was sensational news back then.

1600
01:34:48,039 --> 01:34:51,164
There's a 300 kilometer distance
between the two locations.

1601
01:34:52,450 --> 01:34:53,866
But one guy is behind both the incidents.

1602
01:34:55,231 --> 01:34:57,064
Having a gang is one thing.

1603
01:34:57,232 --> 01:34:58,399
Utilizing them is another.

1604
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:02,667
I'm a free man who is
dead in the police records.

1605
01:35:02,706 --> 01:35:03,826
Practically, a ghost.

1606
01:35:04,675 --> 01:35:08,022
The only person who
can help you at this time.

1607
01:35:08,156 --> 01:35:10,806
Let's say the scam files reach the CM.

1608
01:35:13,914 --> 01:35:14,956
What do you want?

1609
01:35:29,951 --> 01:35:31,184
[glass clinks]

1610
01:35:34,416 --> 01:35:36,083
Can I be of any help?

1611
01:35:37,426 --> 01:35:40,413
Umm... These are all scam files, dear.

1612
01:35:43,233 --> 01:35:44,112
Hold on.

1613
01:35:44,137 --> 01:35:46,137
[papers rustling]

1614
01:35:54,318 --> 01:35:56,032
[intense music playing]

1615
01:36:05,844 --> 01:36:08,078
CM's meeting will be wrapped by 5 PM.

1616
01:36:08,403 --> 01:36:10,516
We will have only 10 minutes of his time.

1617
01:36:10,541 --> 01:36:11,529
You forgot this.

1618
01:36:13,076 --> 01:36:14,521
Everything will go smoothly.

1619
01:36:15,605 --> 01:36:16,396
Let's go.

1620
01:36:20,498 --> 01:36:21,771
[car door clunks]

1621
01:36:28,744 --> 01:36:30,120
Once this symbol goes up,

1622
01:36:30,307 --> 01:36:32,099
everyone in the village knows that...

1623
01:36:32,401 --> 01:36:34,526
a person in that house
has a target on their back.

1624
01:36:34,729 --> 01:36:35,785
[gun shot fired]

1625
01:36:40,776 --> 01:36:42,226
Jhansi, shall we play a game?

1626
01:36:43,039 --> 01:36:44,662
Your family is in danger.

1627
01:36:44,687 --> 01:36:46,914
Will you reveal your identity now...

1628
01:36:47,322 --> 01:36:48,506
or still keep it hidden?

1629
01:36:48,553 --> 01:36:50,553
[alarming music playing]

1630
01:36:59,387 --> 01:37:00,672
Where's Anirudh?

1631
01:37:00,697 --> 01:37:03,394
He went to the hospital.
He asked me to tell you.

1632
01:37:03,834 --> 01:37:04,810
What about Sharath?

1633
01:37:04,835 --> 01:37:07,578
He went to the police station.
The CM meeting is today, remember?

1634
01:37:07,642 --> 01:37:08,731
What happened, love?

1635
01:37:09,351 --> 01:37:11,601
-Nothing. Just asking.
-Sister!

1636
01:37:11,684 --> 01:37:14,142
You said you'd make
Nellore fish curry for everyone.

1637
01:37:14,167 --> 01:37:15,292
I'm kind of busy now.

1638
01:37:15,317 --> 01:37:17,523
Let's make it Swarna.
You know we make a good team.

1639
01:37:17,548 --> 01:37:18,392
You relax.

1640
01:37:18,417 --> 01:37:20,618
You can't make it
better than Swarna.

1641
01:37:20,642 --> 01:37:21,827
Sister, you do the cooking.

1642
01:37:21,851 --> 01:37:23,674
Okay. I'll buy fish and come.

1643
01:37:25,440 --> 01:37:27,573
[vehicle rattling]

1644
01:37:32,272 --> 01:37:35,647
I want to watch and learn
how you pick good fish.

1645
01:37:36,768 --> 01:37:37,726
Let's go?

1646
01:37:38,942 --> 01:37:39,627
Come.

1647
01:37:50,728 --> 01:37:52,791
CM is arriving in 30 minutes.

1648
01:37:53,029 --> 01:37:54,946
Comb the whole area one more time.

1649
01:37:55,140 --> 01:37:58,095
Arrest anyone that you find suspicious.

1650
01:37:58,120 --> 01:37:59,429
Where are we going?

1651
01:38:00,177 --> 01:38:03,184
You're covering the whole
village like you know the place.

1652
01:38:03,551 --> 01:38:04,552
Are you listening?

1653
01:38:06,278 --> 01:38:08,278
[eerie music builds up]

1654
01:38:10,654 --> 01:38:12,553
Who do you think is the target, Jhansi?

1655
01:38:12,770 --> 01:38:15,588
The strongest in the
family should die first.

1656
01:38:15,613 --> 01:38:16,553
Your brother-in-law.

1657
01:38:19,196 --> 01:38:19,988
Agree?

1658
01:38:20,207 --> 01:38:22,040
The fish market is this way.

1659
01:38:23,363 --> 01:38:25,279
-Swarna!
-Which way is the police station?

1660
01:38:25,532 --> 01:38:26,408
That way.

1661
01:38:26,433 --> 01:38:27,310
Stop, stop!

1662
01:38:27,348 --> 01:38:28,355
[tires screech]

1663
01:38:28,380 --> 01:38:30,214
The strongest guy is of no use to us.

1664
01:38:31,027 --> 01:38:33,384
It should be someone whose
death would break your heart.

1665
01:38:33,785 --> 01:38:35,100
Your husband.

1666
01:38:38,075 --> 01:38:39,583
He should be the one to die.

1667
01:38:40,520 --> 01:38:41,562
What's wrong?

1668
01:38:41,750 --> 01:38:44,112
We get better fish
near Anirudh's hospital.

1669
01:38:44,145 --> 01:38:45,353
Let's go there.

1670
01:38:45,703 --> 01:38:47,310
[vehicle engine revving]

1671
01:38:52,376 --> 01:38:53,835
No, that's not right.

1672
01:38:54,158 --> 01:38:57,825
The Head of the Family should die
first, so that the whole family collapses.

1673
01:38:58,059 --> 01:38:59,350
I'll kill him.

1674
01:39:05,295 --> 01:39:06,295
Swarna!

1675
01:39:07,119 --> 01:39:08,119
What happened?

1676
01:39:09,191 --> 01:39:11,191
[suspenseful music playing]

1677
01:39:15,559 --> 01:39:17,851
Why are you going towards the rally?

1678
01:39:19,150 --> 01:39:20,840
I'm talking to you!

1679
01:39:28,519 --> 01:39:30,428
Where did you bring me?

1680
01:39:31,060 --> 01:39:33,412
Swarna, will we find fish here?

1681
01:39:37,162 --> 01:39:39,120
-Hey!
-Hold on.

1682
01:39:40,291 --> 01:39:42,291
[suspenseful music continues]

1683
01:40:05,172 --> 01:40:06,060
Hey!

1684
01:40:06,084 --> 01:40:08,276
Where are you going? Wait for me.

1685
01:40:08,861 --> 01:40:09,898
Hey!

1686
01:40:11,958 --> 01:40:13,214
Are you playing with me?

1687
01:40:13,239 --> 01:40:16,146
What's going on? You're
clearly not here for fish.

1688
01:40:16,170 --> 01:40:17,325
You can't fool me.

1689
01:40:17,349 --> 01:40:20,063
Listen, I have no idea how
to make Nellore fish curry.

1690
01:40:20,087 --> 01:40:21,941
In fact, I can't make any kind of curry.

1691
01:40:21,966 --> 01:40:24,215
Go do whatever you
want with that information.

1692
01:40:26,983 --> 01:40:28,444
Just call for a
rickshaw and go home.

1693
01:40:46,760 --> 01:40:49,073
How long, brother?
We've been here for an hour.

1694
01:40:49,322 --> 01:40:50,748
Let the CM arrive.

1695
01:40:50,773 --> 01:40:52,175
The crowd will go bonkers,

1696
01:40:52,200 --> 01:40:54,227
giving us the perfect opportunity
to nab Ramaiah Raju.

1697
01:41:00,073 --> 01:41:01,480
[footsteps thud]

1698
01:41:08,214 --> 01:41:10,656
-Go back.
-What are you saying?

1699
01:41:11,113 --> 01:41:12,337
Have you lost it?

1700
01:41:12,454 --> 01:41:13,830
Who are you? Get out!

1701
01:41:13,919 --> 01:41:15,605
Let her stay, man. She looks nice.

1702
01:41:16,579 --> 01:41:18,340
I won't be quiet if you
mess with my family.

1703
01:41:18,686 --> 01:41:20,007
Tell this to Karuna.

1704
01:41:20,500 --> 01:41:22,303
Start the bus and go
towards the outskirts.

1705
01:41:22,328 --> 01:41:24,505
Who do you think you are?
Get the hell out!

1706
01:41:25,266 --> 01:41:27,764
You heard him!

1707
01:41:27,901 --> 01:41:29,901
[dramatic music playing]

1708
01:41:36,770 --> 01:41:38,784
[thud]

1709
01:41:40,716 --> 01:41:41,676
Start the bus!

1710
01:41:44,169 --> 01:41:45,377
[gear shifts]

1711
01:41:46,866 --> 01:41:48,362
[knife whooshes]

1712
01:41:48,422 --> 01:41:50,327
[thud sounds continue]

1713
01:41:57,061 --> 01:41:58,977
-Stop the bus!
-Don't stop!

1714
01:42:30,765 --> 01:42:32,454
[glass shattering]

1715
01:42:34,558 --> 01:42:36,357
[bus comes to a halt]

1716
01:42:41,998 --> 01:42:43,499
Keep driving and don't look back.

1717
01:42:45,351 --> 01:42:48,499
-All hail...
-Our beloved CM!

1718
01:42:48,559 --> 01:42:50,517
[sirens blaring]

1719
01:42:50,650 --> 01:42:52,984
[bustling slogans]

1720
01:43:05,087 --> 01:43:06,515
Sir, this has the details...

1721
01:43:06,540 --> 01:43:09,408
pertaining to Madhusudhan
Rao's liquor scam.

1722
01:43:12,949 --> 01:43:13,803
Brother...

1723
01:43:30,156 --> 01:43:33,182
I'm sure you told your
family about your old life.

1724
01:43:33,877 --> 01:43:35,076
You didn't?

1725
01:43:36,098 --> 01:43:37,702
Not even your husband knows?

1726
01:43:39,547 --> 01:43:40,774
That's sad!

1727
01:43:45,406 --> 01:43:48,367
He knows that you haven't
told your family anything.

1728
01:43:48,694 --> 01:43:50,138
He will use that fear against you...

1729
01:43:51,664 --> 01:43:53,129
and play games with you.

1730
01:43:56,026 --> 01:43:57,359
[gun shot fired]

1731
01:44:00,712 --> 01:44:02,313
Your family is in danger.

1732
01:44:02,338 --> 01:44:04,565
Will you reveal your identity now...

1733
01:44:04,821 --> 01:44:06,014
or still keep it hidden?

1734
01:44:06,534 --> 01:44:08,534
[intense music playing]

1735
01:44:19,492 --> 01:44:22,162
Are you sad that the plan failed, Karuna?

1736
01:44:22,630 --> 01:44:26,797
I didn't get out of jail to
be Madhusudhan's puppet.

1737
01:44:27,802 --> 01:44:29,410
Is that how you see me?

1738
01:44:29,947 --> 01:44:32,399
Creating a mess in the
bus with all those men!

1739
01:44:32,505 --> 01:44:34,421
You call that a plan?

1740
01:44:35,015 --> 01:44:38,140
He was stupid to execute it.
But where was your common sense?

1741
01:44:39,972 --> 01:44:43,222
We're slowly making Swarna
realize the Jhansi side of her.

1742
01:44:44,169 --> 01:44:45,753
That's what I'm here for.

1743
01:44:47,494 --> 01:44:49,001
She's just like us.

1744
01:44:50,084 --> 01:44:53,084
You boasted about your bus plan.
But it was one big failure.

1745
01:44:53,213 --> 01:44:56,713
You just added fuel to fire.

1746
01:44:56,854 --> 01:44:58,672
Go on! Enjoy your food!

1747
01:44:59,008 --> 01:45:00,133
The CM has the files now.

1748
01:45:00,183 --> 01:45:01,892
It's over for me.

1749
01:45:02,046 --> 01:45:03,797
The police will be here to arrest me.

1750
01:45:03,891 --> 01:45:04,849
You think I'll let this pass?

1751
01:45:04,958 --> 01:45:06,249
You think?

1752
01:45:06,588 --> 01:45:09,726
If I go to jail, you make
sure to destroy his family.

1753
01:45:09,751 --> 01:45:11,292
None of them should be alive.

1754
01:45:11,755 --> 01:45:12,922
Kill each one of them.

1755
01:45:13,034 --> 01:45:14,409
Take my men if necessary.

1756
01:45:14,666 --> 01:45:15,679
How many men do you need?

1757
01:45:15,751 --> 01:45:17,501
Answer me, damn it!

1758
01:45:18,117 --> 01:45:19,117
Sit down.

1759
01:45:21,528 --> 01:45:22,612
Sit down!

1760
01:45:27,263 --> 01:45:29,430
We'll do everything you just said.

1761
01:45:30,755 --> 01:45:32,505
But I'll decide the time.

1762
01:45:34,421 --> 01:45:37,046
She asked me to leave
and boarded some bus.

1763
01:45:37,088 --> 01:45:41,296
She's a rare fish. You need
a bigger net to catch it.

1764
01:45:42,713 --> 01:45:44,922
I make mind blowing fish curry.

1765
01:45:45,421 --> 01:45:46,505
Should I?

1766
01:45:49,919 --> 01:45:51,222
[sneaky laugh]

1767
01:45:55,630 --> 01:45:57,672
I know why that spatula was bent.

1768
01:46:02,505 --> 01:46:05,797
We figured out what
you and Swarna are up to.

1769
01:46:06,630 --> 01:46:08,838
What are you staring at?

1770
01:46:09,046 --> 01:46:10,005
Speak up!

1771
01:46:10,672 --> 01:46:12,672
Swarna didn't do it on purpose.

1772
01:46:12,978 --> 01:46:14,686
He only fell on the knife.

1773
01:46:14,711 --> 01:46:16,794
Fell on the knife? What are you saying?

1774
01:46:17,171 --> 01:46:19,059
Whose knife, and who fell on it?

1775
01:46:19,298 --> 01:46:21,131
We saw him outside the
house couple of days back.

1776
01:46:21,588 --> 01:46:23,838
But yesterday, he directly
barged into the house.

1777
01:46:24,367 --> 01:46:26,554
As if she doesn't have
enough problems already.

1778
01:46:27,153 --> 01:46:29,028
Yeah, right. What problems?

1779
01:46:31,035 --> 01:46:34,010
Do you know how tough
it is to live in the woods?

1780
01:46:34,077 --> 01:46:35,411
What was she doing in the woods?

1781
01:46:37,445 --> 01:46:40,945
Forget I said that.
That was the old Swarna.

1782
01:46:41,880 --> 01:46:43,880
Old Swarna? As opposed to the new Swarna?

1783
01:46:44,475 --> 01:46:47,922
I don't like this, you
holding me hostage here.

1784
01:46:48,005 --> 01:46:49,171
I'm leaving!

1785
01:46:49,171 --> 01:46:50,296
Stop!

1786
01:46:50,630 --> 01:46:51,588
Come back!

1787
01:46:52,463 --> 01:46:53,505
Old Swarna.

1788
01:46:53,880 --> 01:46:55,088
New Swarna.

1789
01:46:55,996 --> 01:46:57,336
[fax machine buzzing]

1790
01:46:57,366 --> 01:46:59,908
The bus was right there till then.
It was filled with goons.

1791
01:47:01,114 --> 01:47:04,031
I stepped aside to inform
them and the bus was gone.

1792
01:47:04,115 --> 01:47:06,073
I think they were planning something big.

1793
01:47:06,321 --> 01:47:07,733
But then they left for some reason.

1794
01:47:08,422 --> 01:47:09,547
Why did the plan fail?

1795
01:47:11,616 --> 01:47:12,824
Who is behind this?

1796
01:47:16,118 --> 01:47:18,648
[dramatic music playing]

1797
01:47:27,950 --> 01:47:29,032
Swarna?

1798
01:47:36,310 --> 01:47:39,205
Swarna, hold up. I forgot
to tell you something.

1799
01:47:39,374 --> 01:47:42,028
I didn't do it intentionally.
They forced it out of me.

1800
01:47:42,053 --> 01:47:44,888
They took me into the room
and held me hostage. I got scared.

1801
01:47:44,913 --> 01:47:46,494
Whom did you tell?
And what did you tell?

1802
01:47:46,519 --> 01:47:47,935
It was Anasuya and Buchiraju.

1803
01:47:50,407 --> 01:47:52,104
That's the least of my worries.

1804
01:47:52,418 --> 01:47:55,494
I'm more worried about what
Karuna is going to do at the moment.

1805
01:47:58,135 --> 01:47:59,449
Dhatri, come here.

1806
01:48:01,584 --> 01:48:05,043
Now I have to speak to the
one person I didn't want to.

1807
01:48:07,124 --> 01:48:08,205
But he's a cop.

1808
01:48:08,965 --> 01:48:10,605
I'll only tell him what's important.

1809
01:48:21,916 --> 01:48:23,125
I need to talk to you.

1810
01:48:23,456 --> 01:48:24,414
What do you have to say?

1811
01:48:25,951 --> 01:48:28,076
I got hold of your old police records.

1812
01:48:29,505 --> 01:48:31,137
I know everything about you.

1813
01:48:33,114 --> 01:48:34,614
I wouldn't be so sure.

1814
01:48:38,658 --> 01:48:40,658
[upbeat music playing]

1815
01:49:05,669 --> 01:49:06,865
Mr. Raju...

1816
01:49:06,967 --> 01:49:08,092
How are you doing?

1817
01:49:13,511 --> 01:49:14,625
Namaste.

1818
01:49:14,932 --> 01:49:18,474
-Who are you, if I may ask?
-I'm Karuna. Swarna's cousin.

1819
01:49:19,281 --> 01:49:21,668
Oh, you came at a good time.

1820
01:49:21,861 --> 01:49:23,174
Glad to meet you.

1821
01:49:24,446 --> 01:49:26,397
You must have lunch
before you go. I insist.

1822
01:49:27,880 --> 01:49:29,438
Didn't you tell them I was coming?

1823
01:49:29,463 --> 01:49:32,396
Why didn't I know he was coming, dear?

1824
01:49:32,588 --> 01:49:33,546
Kamakshi...

1825
01:49:33,571 --> 01:49:34,404
Come here.

1826
01:49:35,438 --> 01:49:36,854
This is Swarna's cousin.

1827
01:49:36,879 --> 01:49:38,247
That's lovely.

1828
01:49:38,783 --> 01:49:40,023
Did you just arrive?

1829
01:49:40,048 --> 01:49:41,228
I was in the vicinity.

1830
01:49:41,252 --> 01:49:44,298
I thought I'd see Jhan... Swarna and go.

1831
01:49:44,385 --> 01:49:47,411
That's sweet of you.
Please have lunch and go.

1832
01:49:47,588 --> 01:49:49,621
Swarna, please take care of that.

1833
01:49:49,887 --> 01:49:53,041
-Dear, we need you there.
-Let's go.

1834
01:49:53,066 --> 01:49:54,816
-Take care of him, Swarna.
-Hope you enjoy the lunch.

1835
01:49:59,543 --> 01:50:00,543
What is it?

1836
01:50:02,053 --> 01:50:03,129
Do I look nice?

1837
01:50:04,480 --> 01:50:07,399
It's our family function, right?
I had to dress up.

1838
01:50:08,973 --> 01:50:10,973
[water trickling]

1839
01:50:16,524 --> 01:50:17,940
What the hell are you doing, Karuna?

1840
01:50:18,574 --> 01:50:19,782
You gave me your word.

1841
01:50:20,317 --> 01:50:21,609
Why did you come back?

1842
01:50:21,977 --> 01:50:22,852
Come on!

1843
01:50:23,650 --> 01:50:26,109
You've been going on and on about family.

1844
01:50:26,317 --> 01:50:29,817
I came to see what the hype is about.

1845
01:50:29,984 --> 01:50:35,261
Watching all this, I feel
like I want a family too.

1846
01:50:35,766 --> 01:50:36,653
Swarna!

1847
01:50:41,650 --> 01:50:42,526
Is this your husband?

1848
01:50:43,276 --> 01:50:45,900
Swarna, you didn't tell me
your brother was coming.

1849
01:50:45,942 --> 01:50:47,025
Cousin.

1850
01:50:52,859 --> 01:50:54,067
Where's the lunch being served?

1851
01:50:55,317 --> 01:50:56,764
Please follow me.

1852
01:50:58,939 --> 01:51:00,939
[eerie music playing]

1853
01:51:04,165 --> 01:51:05,997
Look. Who is that?

1854
01:51:06,022 --> 01:51:07,481
Swarna's cousin.

1855
01:51:09,424 --> 01:51:12,216
We'll know everything if we talk to him.

1856
01:51:13,484 --> 01:51:15,984
You also come sit with me.
I saved a chair for you.

1857
01:51:16,484 --> 01:51:18,049
It's been a while since we ate together.

1858
01:51:18,165 --> 01:51:19,082
Go talk to him.

1859
01:51:19,109 --> 01:51:20,067
Let her leave.

1860
01:51:20,276 --> 01:51:21,234
Come, come.

1861
01:51:24,650 --> 01:51:26,202
[smiles awkwardly] Namaste.

1862
01:51:26,733 --> 01:51:28,310
I'm Buchiraju.
She's Anasuya.

1863
01:51:28,334 --> 01:51:30,917
Namaste. Here's some brinjal curry.

1864
01:51:30,942 --> 01:51:33,141
We heard you're Swarna's close family.

1865
01:51:33,166 --> 01:51:34,619
You know her since childhood, right?

1866
01:51:34,643 --> 01:51:35,608
What do you want?

1867
01:51:36,650 --> 01:51:40,775
Swarna hasn't told us
anything about her childhood.

1868
01:51:40,939 --> 01:51:42,565
So, we thought we would ask you.

1869
01:51:43,276 --> 01:51:44,442
A lot has happened.

1870
01:51:44,467 --> 01:51:45,634
We're all ears!

1871
01:51:47,401 --> 01:51:49,253
Things that happened to
her or things that she did?

1872
01:51:49,317 --> 01:51:50,348
What do you want to know?

1873
01:51:50,543 --> 01:51:52,126
Both sides are terrifying.

1874
01:51:56,192 --> 01:51:57,355
Swarna, come here!

1875
01:52:02,605 --> 01:52:04,148
[eerie music playing]

1876
01:52:07,401 --> 01:52:09,900
Taste the brinjal. It's nice.

1877
01:52:10,374 --> 01:52:12,302
What's that? Give me some.

1878
01:52:14,526 --> 01:52:15,775
I have a lot of work to do.

1879
01:52:15,817 --> 01:52:17,502
The sambar is yummy. Have it.

1880
01:52:17,527 --> 01:52:18,876
Alright. Give me some.

1881
01:52:21,006 --> 01:52:22,215
Give me two vegetable pieces.

1882
01:52:25,609 --> 01:52:27,229
Exactly two?

1883
01:52:30,526 --> 01:52:32,609
I'll serve. You go.

1884
01:52:36,650 --> 01:52:37,775
There you go.

1885
01:52:42,204 --> 01:52:43,117
Is it enough?

1886
01:53:07,794 --> 01:53:09,474
[eerie music continues]

1887
01:53:20,733 --> 01:53:23,331
Sister-in-law, let's click a picture?

1888
01:53:31,745 --> 01:53:33,662
Swarna's cousin, right?

1889
01:53:34,495 --> 01:53:35,745
Are you married?

1890
01:53:39,317 --> 01:53:40,131
We're ready.

1891
01:53:41,150 --> 01:53:42,848
You look lovely.

1892
01:53:42,900 --> 01:53:45,817
Let me find a girl for you.
Do you have any preferences?

1893
01:53:48,461 --> 01:53:49,919
Let's click against this background.

1894
01:53:55,775 --> 01:53:56,650
Swarna.

1895
01:53:57,526 --> 01:53:58,783
Someone like Swarna.

1896
01:53:59,588 --> 01:54:02,129
Grandma, aunt is looking for you.

1897
01:54:02,775 --> 01:54:03,692
Go.

1898
01:54:08,192 --> 01:54:10,192
You left me hanging back there.

1899
01:54:10,234 --> 01:54:11,526
Finish the story, please?

1900
01:54:11,561 --> 01:54:14,060
You said it's terrifying and all.

1901
01:54:14,109 --> 01:54:15,192
Sister-in-law, face the camera.

1902
01:54:15,768 --> 01:54:17,264
[camera shutter clicks]

1903
01:54:17,905 --> 01:54:19,275
[knuckles crack]

1904
01:54:19,942 --> 01:54:23,526
Well, don't you think you
should finish the story?

1905
01:54:23,705 --> 01:54:26,306
I'll break your bones
if you keep sticking...

1906
01:54:26,634 --> 01:54:27,875
your nose into everything.

1907
01:54:27,900 --> 01:54:28,900
Understood?

1908
01:54:29,613 --> 01:54:30,780
Yes, yes.

1909
01:54:38,839 --> 01:54:40,519
Are you feeling sleepy?

1910
01:54:48,192 --> 01:54:49,234
Jhansi!

1911
01:54:50,317 --> 01:54:51,109
Jhansi!

1912
01:54:53,307 --> 01:54:54,182
Jhansi!

1913
01:54:58,844 --> 01:55:00,052
You better leave!

1914
01:55:01,067 --> 01:55:03,526
You told a million
lies to enter this family.

1915
01:55:03,561 --> 01:55:06,399
Yet, you're threatening me openly.

1916
01:55:06,423 --> 01:55:08,256
Very dramatic!

1917
01:55:10,109 --> 01:55:12,109
This is why I like you.

1918
01:55:14,135 --> 01:55:15,051
I said leave!

1919
01:55:15,650 --> 01:55:16,984
Alright, I will.

1920
01:55:18,234 --> 01:55:20,775
-I came here to tell you something.
-Don't yell!

1921
01:55:22,080 --> 01:55:24,544
Should I tell you here or in private?

1922
01:55:37,245 --> 01:55:38,425
What is it?

1923
01:55:40,279 --> 01:55:41,335
[thud]

1924
01:55:41,360 --> 01:55:42,713
[gasping]

1925
01:55:43,102 --> 01:55:45,716
Will you finally drop the act now?

1926
01:55:47,663 --> 01:55:48,774
[grunts]

1927
01:55:50,359 --> 01:55:52,036
What the hell are you doing, Jhansi?

1928
01:55:53,340 --> 01:55:56,574
Serving sambar to everyone.

1929
01:55:56,849 --> 01:55:58,585
You think this is what you're meant to do?

1930
01:56:00,393 --> 01:56:01,704
[spits]

1931
01:56:07,102 --> 01:56:11,983
I revived a dying person
and nurtured her. That's you!

1932
01:56:12,563 --> 01:56:16,960
If there's anything special
about you, it's because of me.

1933
01:56:17,865 --> 01:56:19,562
Now you'll leave me for family?

1934
01:56:20,568 --> 01:56:22,323
What's so great about a family?

1935
01:56:22,347 --> 01:56:24,283
Everyone in this world does this.

1936
01:56:25,526 --> 01:56:29,775
Love, marriage, baby shower, kids.

1937
01:56:29,942 --> 01:56:32,731
Removing their lice,
washing their asses.

1938
01:56:34,848 --> 01:56:36,407
You came back to life for this?

1939
01:56:47,256 --> 01:56:52,381
Most of us live in a
bubble and die in a bubble.

1940
01:56:54,507 --> 01:56:56,341
Quit this cooking nonsense.

1941
01:56:56,603 --> 01:56:58,614
Meditate for 5 minutes.

1942
01:56:59,844 --> 01:57:02,468
You'll realize what you're doing in life.

1943
01:57:02,806 --> 01:57:05,049
Swarna... Swarna...

1944
01:57:06,338 --> 01:57:09,690
Your devoted husband
is looking for you. Go.

1945
01:57:14,529 --> 01:57:16,554
I was planning to kill your husband,

1946
01:57:16,579 --> 01:57:19,720
your in-laws, and everyone else.

1947
01:57:19,748 --> 01:57:21,488
But I'm giving you one last chance.

1948
01:57:21,938 --> 01:57:23,607
Once you're done here, come back to me.

1949
01:57:26,140 --> 01:57:27,621
[creepy laugh]

1950
01:57:29,856 --> 01:57:31,147
I came to your house,

1951
01:57:31,786 --> 01:57:33,911
had lunch among everyone,

1952
01:57:33,936 --> 01:57:37,515
and now I'm talking
to you in your bedroom.

1953
01:57:38,693 --> 01:57:41,819
Think about what else I can do.

1954
01:57:42,986 --> 01:57:43,735
Go.

1955
01:57:45,433 --> 01:57:46,247
Oi!

1956
01:57:47,358 --> 01:57:48,906
If you don't come,

1957
01:57:48,931 --> 01:57:50,707
I'll come for all their lives.

1958
01:57:50,792 --> 01:57:52,955
Pack your bags tonight and come to me.

1959
01:57:54,330 --> 01:57:55,914
Swarna...

1960
01:57:56,525 --> 01:57:58,279
-Where were you?
-I was right here.

1961
01:57:58,529 --> 01:57:59,487
I'll be back.

1962
01:58:01,176 --> 01:58:02,010
Ani!

1963
01:58:03,909 --> 01:58:06,396
Can you get me a ride to
the bus stop? I'm running late.

1964
01:58:07,936 --> 01:58:09,758
[bike revs]

1965
01:58:19,431 --> 01:58:21,379
[intense music sets in]

1966
01:58:50,356 --> 01:58:51,731
Do you think she will show up, Karuna?

1967
01:58:53,254 --> 01:58:55,489
I explained it to her slowly and sweetly,

1968
01:58:55,513 --> 01:58:57,095
in a way she would understood.

1969
01:58:58,890 --> 01:59:00,080
She will show up.

1970
01:59:00,424 --> 01:59:01,701
She has no choice.

1971
01:59:03,350 --> 01:59:05,209
[footsteps thudding]

1972
01:59:25,522 --> 01:59:27,522
[melancholic music playing]

1973
01:59:28,107 --> 01:59:29,882
Take this tablet in the morning.

1974
01:59:35,216 --> 01:59:37,216
[dramatic music playing]

1975
01:59:53,271 --> 01:59:54,938
Ever since I have been with you,

1976
01:59:55,554 --> 01:59:57,470
I have started liking myself.

1977
01:59:58,194 --> 02:00:00,028
I was scared that if you
find out about my past,

1978
02:00:01,710 --> 02:00:04,752
you wouldn't look at me the same anymore.

1979
02:00:07,157 --> 02:00:09,073
Maybe you would've understood.

1980
02:00:09,734 --> 02:00:10,710
But I...

1981
02:00:12,436 --> 02:00:13,712
I didn't have the courage.

1982
02:00:15,442 --> 02:00:18,150
The fact that you didn't
tell me any of this...

1983
02:00:19,988 --> 02:00:21,527
hurts me more.

1984
02:00:22,587 --> 02:00:24,515
[melancholic music playing]

1985
02:00:44,605 --> 02:00:46,368
[bike revs]

1986
02:01:43,623 --> 02:01:44,923
Swarna, hold on.

1987
02:01:45,382 --> 02:01:46,722
What do we do about Karuna?

1988
02:01:49,449 --> 02:01:50,491
Our fight isn't over.

1989
02:01:51,182 --> 02:01:52,353
I'm still angry.

1990
02:01:53,967 --> 02:01:55,536
But let's deal with him first...

1991
02:01:55,993 --> 02:01:57,448
and go back to our argument.

1992
02:01:59,596 --> 02:02:00,904
I'll talk to my dad.

1993
02:02:01,998 --> 02:02:03,748
He knows some big names.

1994
02:02:04,582 --> 02:02:06,319
Or we could talk to the police.

1995
02:02:07,526 --> 02:02:08,693
I did already.

1996
02:02:10,605 --> 02:02:12,118
I spoke to Sharath.

1997
02:02:14,493 --> 02:02:15,793
I need to talk to you.

1998
02:02:16,594 --> 02:02:18,103
I know you have no reason to believe me.

1999
02:02:18,396 --> 02:02:20,438
But we have a huge danger coming our way.

2000
02:02:20,644 --> 02:02:22,144
Only you can help us.

2001
02:02:23,383 --> 02:02:24,508
Without any evidence?

2002
02:02:24,707 --> 02:02:25,831
There is evidence.

2003
02:02:26,092 --> 02:02:27,509
Let's click against this background.

2004
02:02:33,139 --> 02:02:34,139
Sir, Sharath here.

2005
02:02:34,422 --> 02:02:35,668
He is alive, sir.

2006
02:02:35,693 --> 02:02:37,152
I'm sending the evidence right now.

2007
02:02:40,567 --> 02:02:42,509
Give this at the DSP's
office. It's urgent.

2008
02:02:44,814 --> 02:02:46,938
I wish everything went to plan.

2009
02:02:47,403 --> 02:02:49,897
But Karuna is unpredictable.

2010
02:02:51,873 --> 02:02:55,046
If something goes wrong,
our family will be targeted.

2011
02:02:57,526 --> 02:02:58,445
Ani...

2012
02:03:00,021 --> 02:03:01,100
I'll walk away.

2013
02:03:02,216 --> 02:03:03,250
That's better.

2014
02:03:05,175 --> 02:03:07,469
Why did you fight for my family then?

2015
02:03:09,021 --> 02:03:10,141
Your family?

2016
02:03:10,554 --> 02:03:12,137
They're my family too.

2017
02:03:12,836 --> 02:03:13,795
Exactly!

2018
02:03:14,647 --> 02:03:17,353
Then how can you walk away?

2019
02:03:18,271 --> 02:03:19,896
You fought alone this whole time.

2020
02:03:20,803 --> 02:03:22,379
But now you have me.

2021
02:03:23,878 --> 02:03:24,922
We'll handle this together.

2022
02:03:25,470 --> 02:03:27,399
[emotional music playing]

2023
02:03:36,615 --> 02:03:38,615
[wedding bells ringing]

2024
02:03:52,371 --> 02:03:54,371
[suspenseful music sets in]

2025
02:04:28,098 --> 02:04:28,877
The job is done.

2026
02:04:28,901 --> 02:04:30,802
We're moving him to
the Central Jail tonight.

2027
02:04:35,781 --> 02:04:37,578
Yes, sir. We just got the arrest warrant.

2028
02:04:37,679 --> 02:04:39,679
[sirens blaring]

2029
02:05:12,525 --> 02:05:15,563
Let's put this behind us.

2030
02:05:16,029 --> 02:05:17,196
It's over now.

2031
02:05:18,230 --> 02:05:19,146
No, Ani.

2032
02:05:20,188 --> 02:05:21,730
There's one last thing that I need to do.

2033
02:05:27,002 --> 02:05:29,002
[vehicle engine revs]

2034
02:05:42,998 --> 02:05:44,998
[eerie music sets in]

2035
02:05:45,790 --> 02:05:47,494
[handcuffs clinking]

2036
02:05:47,930 --> 02:05:49,218
[gun shots fired]

2037
02:05:49,242 --> 02:05:52,301
[vehicle thuds and crashes]

2038
02:06:12,157 --> 02:06:13,999
Why did you hide the truth for so long?

2039
02:06:16,085 --> 02:06:17,586
To be honest,

2040
02:06:18,441 --> 02:06:20,108
I didn't have the courage to do it.

2041
02:06:22,663 --> 02:06:25,496
A lie gave me such a
beautiful family that...

2042
02:06:27,742 --> 02:06:29,951
I didn't mind hiding the truth.

2043
02:06:30,445 --> 02:06:32,380
Why are you coming clean now?

2044
02:06:33,200 --> 02:06:35,582
I thought my past was my problem.

2045
02:06:36,312 --> 02:06:40,312
But the same past has
come to haunt my family now.

2046
02:06:42,656 --> 02:06:45,114
We were happy to
welcome you into the family.

2047
02:06:45,391 --> 02:06:49,516
But now you're talking guns and forests.

2048
02:06:50,511 --> 02:06:52,427
I don't even know what to make of it.

2049
02:06:58,021 --> 02:07:03,244
I've never had anyone
that I could call family.

2050
02:07:05,371 --> 02:07:06,954
Nobody taught me anything.

2051
02:07:09,431 --> 02:07:13,098
I learned from my personal
mistakes, challenges and betrayals.

2052
02:07:13,710 --> 02:07:15,293
I taught myself everything I know.

2053
02:07:16,815 --> 02:07:18,398
I'm not defending myself here.

2054
02:07:18,732 --> 02:07:20,451
I'm just telling you how things were.

2055
02:07:23,994 --> 02:07:27,558
You treated me like your own,
though I was an outsider.

2056
02:07:28,652 --> 02:07:32,444
I experienced what it's like to
have a family for this short period.

2057
02:07:36,435 --> 02:07:38,352
But it often dawned upon me that...

2058
02:07:39,252 --> 02:07:40,864
a dishonest person like me...

2059
02:07:41,734 --> 02:07:44,562
isn't deserving of the
'daughter-in-law' title in your family.

2060
02:07:46,772 --> 02:07:51,189
I saw a matrimonial ad
looking for a bride once.

2061
02:07:52,558 --> 02:07:54,679
She should be beautiful, soft-spoken,

2062
02:07:54,704 --> 02:07:57,620
be able to cook, sing and sew, they said.

2063
02:07:57,892 --> 02:07:59,351
It was a long list.

2064
02:08:01,622 --> 02:08:06,295
A daughter-in-law should have all
these qualities to be the ideal woman.

2065
02:08:07,108 --> 02:08:08,941
But I had none of those.

2066
02:08:10,551 --> 02:08:12,272
If everyone were the best,

2067
02:08:12,297 --> 02:08:15,260
there's no chance a person
like me would find a good home.

2068
02:08:16,302 --> 02:08:17,511
But then,

2069
02:08:19,063 --> 02:08:20,313
I met Ani.

2070
02:08:23,092 --> 02:08:26,147
He let me be my authentic self.

2071
02:08:26,296 --> 02:08:28,225
[melancholic music playing]

2072
02:08:31,607 --> 02:08:32,925
[crying]

2073
02:08:37,359 --> 02:08:39,068
But if you really think about it,

2074
02:08:39,663 --> 02:08:41,246
I do have one quality.

2075
02:08:41,934 --> 02:08:44,851
Come what may,

2076
02:08:45,330 --> 02:08:49,497
I would risk my life to protect my family.

2077
02:08:53,779 --> 02:08:56,404
Maybe this isn't an ideal
quality for a daughter-in-law.

2078
02:08:57,916 --> 02:09:01,617
Everyone wants to welcome the Goddess
of Prosperity into their home but...

2079
02:09:03,217 --> 02:09:04,424
Answer this.

2080
02:09:04,457 --> 02:09:06,332
You posed a major threat to this family.

2081
02:09:06,698 --> 02:09:07,907
What do you have to say to that?

2082
02:09:08,434 --> 02:09:12,605
Even I posed a major threat to
this family due to my political career.

2083
02:09:13,091 --> 02:09:15,002
But nobody questioned me then.

2084
02:09:16,006 --> 02:09:19,093
Did you forget that she
saved everyone the other day?

2085
02:09:19,547 --> 02:09:21,630
We called her family when she saved us.

2086
02:09:21,664 --> 02:09:23,998
But when things got risky,
you want to abandon her?

2087
02:09:24,203 --> 02:09:25,917
[dramatic music playing]

2088
02:09:28,199 --> 02:09:30,717
Not everyone needs to
be a Goddess of Prosperity.

2089
02:09:30,908 --> 02:09:32,350
Goddess of Destruction exists too.

2090
02:09:35,586 --> 02:09:36,586
[fuse blows]

2091
02:09:36,610 --> 02:09:37,855
[gasps]

2092
02:09:45,131 --> 02:09:46,837
Hey, get the lantern.

2093
02:09:49,899 --> 02:09:51,106
What's going on?

2094
02:09:51,655 --> 02:09:53,072
Something is about to go down.

2095
02:09:53,956 --> 02:09:56,456
I was really sad listening to all that.

2096
02:09:56,481 --> 02:10:00,069
I'm sorry for pestering
with you many questions.

2097
02:10:00,094 --> 02:10:01,343
It's okay, Anasuya.

2098
02:10:01,368 --> 02:10:03,160
I didn't take any of it to heart.

2099
02:10:06,211 --> 02:10:07,731
Umm... listen.

2100
02:10:07,756 --> 02:10:11,949
I bothered you a lot about
your recipes, rangolis, and so on.

2101
02:10:11,974 --> 02:10:14,549
-Please forgive me.
-Anasuya, listen. We're friends now.

2102
02:10:14,607 --> 02:10:16,717
We'll discuss this later, okay?
Please don't mind.

2103
02:10:18,032 --> 02:10:19,956
We're friends too.

2104
02:10:21,997 --> 02:10:23,031
I'll go talk to her.

2105
02:10:33,692 --> 02:10:35,640
[vehicles revving]

2106
02:10:42,930 --> 02:10:44,667
They're Madhusudhan Rao's men.

2107
02:10:46,178 --> 02:10:48,178
[thud]

2108
02:10:48,746 --> 02:10:50,479
[knife whooshes]

2109
02:10:50,635 --> 02:10:52,486
[thud sounds continue]

2110
02:10:57,128 --> 02:10:59,432
[glass shatters]

2111
02:10:59,457 --> 02:11:01,157
[screams]

2112
02:11:02,354 --> 02:11:03,709
Get water!

2113
02:11:03,960 --> 02:11:05,137
[screams]

2114
02:11:05,464 --> 02:11:07,464
[glass bottles clinking]

2115
02:11:07,811 --> 02:11:08,771
Brother, careful!

2116
02:11:10,991 --> 02:11:12,843
[fire fizzes out]

2117
02:11:15,591 --> 02:11:16,471
Don't be scared.

2118
02:11:17,236 --> 02:11:18,111
Do you think they left?

2119
02:11:18,136 --> 02:11:20,581
Let's get out of here before it's late.

2120
02:11:22,511 --> 02:11:23,678
The trouble has just begun.

2121
02:11:23,692 --> 02:11:25,692
[suspenseful music playing]

2122
02:11:45,357 --> 02:11:48,437
Guys, go in there and
put on a good show me.

2123
02:11:48,478 --> 02:11:50,455
I'll be watching from here.

2124
02:11:50,861 --> 02:11:52,402
Listen to me carefully.

2125
02:11:52,461 --> 02:11:53,795
Nobody is going to get hurt.

2126
02:11:54,340 --> 02:11:56,550
First, we need to close
all the doors and windows.

2127
02:11:56,575 --> 02:11:57,890
Yeah, let's do that.

2128
02:11:58,324 --> 02:12:01,427
If we do that, we won't be able
to tell where they're entering from.

2129
02:12:03,189 --> 02:12:05,314
You're right. Let's keep them all open.

2130
02:12:06,006 --> 02:12:08,131
Then they will enter from all sides.

2131
02:12:10,347 --> 02:12:12,347
Alright. You tell us what to do.

2132
02:12:12,954 --> 02:12:13,830
Go ahead.

2133
02:12:15,070 --> 02:12:16,574
They're just trying to scare us.

2134
02:12:17,447 --> 02:12:18,988
If we panic,

2135
02:12:19,230 --> 02:12:21,021
they'll barge in and attack all of us.

2136
02:12:21,212 --> 02:12:22,750
Karuna will play this out like a game.

2137
02:12:22,862 --> 02:12:24,125
That's how he operates.

2138
02:12:24,737 --> 02:12:27,162
So no matter what, we
need to stick together.

2139
02:12:27,685 --> 02:12:29,268
Yeah, but what do we do?

2140
02:12:29,360 --> 02:12:31,546
First, we need to close
all the doors and windows.

2141
02:12:31,570 --> 02:12:32,987
That's what I said.

2142
02:12:33,668 --> 02:12:35,017
Except for this door.

2143
02:12:39,886 --> 02:12:41,886
[door creaks open]

2144
02:12:45,445 --> 02:12:47,382
We'll hide the elderly and
the children in the corner room.

2145
02:12:47,407 --> 02:12:49,812
Hurry up! Get into the bedroom, fast!

2146
02:12:49,837 --> 02:12:50,796
Grandma...

2147
02:12:50,874 --> 02:12:52,601
Gather all the weapons we have.

2148
02:12:52,665 --> 02:12:54,040
What weapons are you talking about?

2149
02:12:54,214 --> 02:12:56,563
Knifes, crowbars, pestles, ladles,

2150
02:12:56,625 --> 02:12:57,917
Whatever you can find, basically.

2151
02:12:57,958 --> 02:13:00,343
Come on, guys! Grab whatever you can.

2152
02:13:00,459 --> 02:13:03,003
-Does a sickle work?
-Perfectly.

2153
02:13:03,027 --> 02:13:04,070
-What about a ladle?
-Works.

2154
02:13:05,134 --> 02:13:05,865
Hurry up!

2155
02:13:05,890 --> 02:13:07,011
We'll make chilli bombs.

2156
02:13:07,035 --> 02:13:09,189
Wrap chilli powder in small packets.

2157
02:13:09,214 --> 02:13:10,238
[knife whooshes]

2158
02:13:10,253 --> 02:13:10,972
[gasps]

2159
02:13:10,996 --> 02:13:14,836
It's time to go sever their heads!

2160
02:13:16,022 --> 02:13:17,353
You all hide safely.

2161
02:13:17,378 --> 02:13:19,170
I'll be back with their severed heads.

2162
02:13:19,599 --> 02:13:21,599
[suspenseful music intensifies]

2163
02:13:25,022 --> 02:13:26,606
Where the hell are you going?

2164
02:13:27,481 --> 02:13:29,398
Swarna is alone. I need to go help her.

2165
02:13:29,939 --> 02:13:30,867
Oh, no!

2166
02:13:30,892 --> 02:13:32,023
[door shuts]

2167
02:13:33,690 --> 02:13:35,113
Go, get in.

2168
02:13:37,734 --> 02:13:39,342
Get me a cup of tea.

2169
02:13:42,757 --> 02:13:45,949
-Don't move, guys.
-I got this. Be careful.

2170
02:13:46,230 --> 02:13:47,954
Be safe. Don't leave this room.

2171
02:13:47,979 --> 02:13:49,136
Lord, help us!

2172
02:13:54,110 --> 02:13:55,265
[door creaks]

2173
02:14:02,625 --> 02:14:04,192
Hey, come this way!

2174
02:14:13,333 --> 02:14:15,333
[door creaking]

2175
02:14:16,481 --> 02:14:18,344
Father-in-law, let them in.

2176
02:14:22,595 --> 02:14:24,595
[gun shots fired]

2177
02:14:25,686 --> 02:14:27,281
You bunch of idiots!

2178
02:14:27,305 --> 02:14:29,632
Why did you enter without a plan?

2179
02:14:30,419 --> 02:14:31,482
[fuse crackles]

2180
02:14:31,506 --> 02:14:34,074
Attack at once!

2181
02:14:34,330 --> 02:14:36,330
[thud]

2182
02:14:38,351 --> 02:14:40,358
Dad, come here.

2183
02:14:45,354 --> 02:14:46,509
[door clunks]

2184
02:14:47,119 --> 02:14:50,501
-Oh, no! What happened?
-Don't worry. He'll be fine.

2185
02:14:50,632 --> 02:14:53,645
-What happened to you?
-Dad, sit down.

2186
02:14:56,494 --> 02:14:58,077
Fight me if you can!

2187
02:14:58,102 --> 02:15:00,294
I'll show you who Buchiraju is.

2188
02:15:00,531 --> 02:15:02,531
[intense music playing]

2189
02:15:27,849 --> 02:15:30,023
[pot breaks]

2190
02:15:36,969 --> 02:15:38,539
[thud]

2191
02:15:38,576 --> 02:15:40,006
[metal clanking]

2192
02:15:46,648 --> 02:15:47,853
[thud sounds continue]

2193
02:15:47,877 --> 02:15:49,795
[music intensifies]

2194
02:15:58,902 --> 02:15:59,909
Sister!

2195
02:16:00,369 --> 02:16:01,369
Help me!

2196
02:16:04,464 --> 02:16:05,479
Help!

2197
02:16:10,669 --> 02:16:11,627
Thanks, sister.

2198
02:16:12,634 --> 02:16:14,683
Get inside. Go!

2199
02:16:20,236 --> 02:16:22,147
[thud sounds continue]

2200
02:16:24,081 --> 02:16:26,039
You asked what she
was doing in the forest?

2201
02:16:27,453 --> 02:16:28,370
Now you know.

2202
02:16:29,435 --> 02:16:31,477
So, she is a good girl...

2203
02:16:31,818 --> 02:16:33,655
with a bad past.

2204
02:16:38,090 --> 02:16:39,549
[furniture breaks]

2205
02:16:39,996 --> 02:16:41,104
Get inside.

2206
02:16:46,465 --> 02:16:48,361
[gasps] He's coming.

2207
02:16:52,971 --> 02:16:54,651
[thud sounds continue]

2208
02:16:55,366 --> 02:16:58,506
I'll pluck your eyeballs, you idiot!

2209
02:17:00,766 --> 02:17:04,166
The bleeding is under control.
Just try to relax.

2210
02:17:27,291 --> 02:17:29,499
What a bunch of losers!

2211
02:17:30,062 --> 02:17:31,747
They want to be these badass goons.

2212
02:17:31,772 --> 02:17:34,344
But they can't fight to save their life.

2213
02:17:39,171 --> 02:17:41,178
[thud sounds continue]

2214
02:17:42,134 --> 02:17:43,370
[grunts]

2215
02:17:59,409 --> 02:18:00,623
[furniture breaks]

2216
02:18:00,661 --> 02:18:02,401
[revolver clicks]

2217
02:18:05,120 --> 02:18:07,120
[music intensifies]

2218
02:18:08,484 --> 02:18:09,883
[thud]

2219
02:18:14,568 --> 02:18:15,930
[gun shot fired]

2220
02:18:21,858 --> 02:18:23,233
Bro, the guns are here!

2221
02:18:26,287 --> 02:18:27,662
So you finally decided to show up?

2222
02:18:28,767 --> 02:18:30,968
Get in there! Now!

2223
02:18:37,776 --> 02:18:39,368
[gun shots firing]

2224
02:18:39,709 --> 02:18:40,982
[door creaks]

2225
02:18:49,569 --> 02:18:50,694
Come with me.

2226
02:18:50,719 --> 02:18:53,358
Let's block that door with a table.

2227
02:18:56,386 --> 02:18:57,323
Flip it.

2228
02:19:07,756 --> 02:19:10,416
-Come, let's go!
-Follow me, guys.

2229
02:19:11,406 --> 02:19:12,467
Watch out!

2230
02:19:17,576 --> 02:19:19,576
[suspenseful music playing]

2231
02:19:20,580 --> 02:19:22,580
[gun shots continue]

2232
02:19:27,177 --> 02:19:28,081
Swarna...

2233
02:19:28,106 --> 02:19:29,266
Should we escape from the back?

2234
02:19:29,384 --> 02:19:30,473
[groans]

2235
02:19:41,235 --> 02:19:42,546
[knife whooshes]

2236
02:19:43,816 --> 02:19:44,816
Sharath!

2237
02:19:47,063 --> 02:19:49,367
[groans]

2238
02:19:54,713 --> 02:19:55,713
Dad!

2239
02:19:57,189 --> 02:20:00,797
Don't worry, Sharath. We got you.

2240
02:20:04,090 --> 02:20:07,492
-What happened?
-Stop panicking and grab a cloth.

2241
02:20:08,467 --> 02:20:10,217
Hurry up! He's bleeding.

2242
02:20:10,616 --> 02:20:12,087
Sharath, just hang in there.

2243
02:20:13,056 --> 02:20:14,142
Press on it.

2244
02:20:15,307 --> 02:20:17,279
Guys, you need to leave right now!

2245
02:20:17,726 --> 02:20:19,471
Hurry up! We don't have time.

2246
02:20:19,556 --> 02:20:20,931
What about you, Swarna?

2247
02:20:20,956 --> 02:20:22,198
You guys leave first.

2248
02:20:22,223 --> 02:20:25,241
-We can't leave you and go.
-You said we should stick together.

2249
02:20:25,265 --> 02:20:27,473
I know. But I need you to go.
I will see you soon.

2250
02:20:27,515 --> 02:20:29,890
Ani, get them out safely.

2251
02:20:30,856 --> 02:20:32,278
Why are you being stubborn?

2252
02:20:33,348 --> 02:20:36,702
Ani, I'll hold the fort here.
You get them out from the back door.

2253
02:20:36,727 --> 02:20:38,512
I'll be with you shortly. Please go.

2254
02:20:38,537 --> 02:20:39,850
How can we leave her behind?

2255
02:20:41,570 --> 02:20:43,533
[gun shots continue]

2256
02:20:47,362 --> 02:20:48,663
Hurry up!

2257
02:20:50,891 --> 02:20:52,451
Hurry up!

2258
02:20:52,780 --> 02:20:53,913
Come, come!

2259
02:20:54,657 --> 02:20:56,545
Guys, hurry!

2260
02:20:59,344 --> 02:21:00,958
Swarna, come quickly.

2261
02:21:00,992 --> 02:21:02,992
[melancholic music playing]

2262
02:21:05,103 --> 02:21:06,466
[gun shots continue]

2263
02:21:13,318 --> 02:21:14,825
He lost a lot of blood.
He needs you there.

2264
02:21:14,850 --> 02:21:17,376
I'll be with Swarna. You go.

2265
02:21:17,400 --> 02:21:19,088
Okay. Be careful.

2266
02:21:22,382 --> 02:21:23,923
I brought some more bullets for you.

2267
02:21:24,410 --> 02:21:25,626
Do you know how to load a gun?

2268
02:21:25,876 --> 02:21:28,542
I watched too many action
movies to not know. Watch me slay!

2269
02:21:30,147 --> 02:21:31,147
I'm back, sister!

2270
02:21:36,556 --> 02:21:38,018
Let's come on!

2271
02:21:38,439 --> 02:21:40,305
[intense music playing]

2272
02:21:40,964 --> 02:21:42,853
[gun shots continue]

2273
02:21:52,090 --> 02:21:53,613
[groans]

2274
02:21:53,637 --> 02:21:54,679
Sister...

2275
02:21:54,704 --> 02:21:57,621
-Oh, no! Are you okay?
-Give me the gun.

2276
02:21:57,845 --> 02:22:00,470
-There are only two bullets.
-How will you manage?

2277
02:22:00,928 --> 02:22:03,092
-You guys go!
-We can't leave without you.

2278
02:22:03,117 --> 02:22:04,012
I said, go!

2279
02:22:04,037 --> 02:22:05,578
I'll join you soon. Just go!

2280
02:22:06,778 --> 02:22:08,124
-Come.
-Be careful.

2281
02:22:09,866 --> 02:22:11,073
[groans]

2282
02:22:19,589 --> 02:22:21,269
[gun shots continue]

2283
02:22:24,672 --> 02:22:28,048
I've created a monster with my own hands.

2284
02:22:50,526 --> 02:22:52,474
[vehicle engine revs]

2285
02:23:16,488 --> 02:23:18,488
[vehicle storming in]

2286
02:23:18,806 --> 02:23:20,806
[wall shatters]

2287
02:23:25,186 --> 02:23:26,341
[groans]

2288
02:23:39,204 --> 02:23:40,819
[shrieks in pain]

2289
02:23:47,564 --> 02:23:49,505
Do I really need this right now?

2290
02:23:51,001 --> 02:23:54,515
Breaking into your house
by tearing the walls down.

2291
02:23:55,213 --> 02:23:57,255
I told you, didn't I?

2292
02:23:57,525 --> 02:24:00,215
This whole family thing
won't work out for you.

2293
02:24:01,301 --> 02:24:02,509
But you were adamant.

2294
02:24:02,607 --> 02:24:03,871
Now look.

2295
02:24:04,779 --> 02:24:07,739
You rained hell on the wedding house.

2296
02:24:08,956 --> 02:24:10,252
[thud]

2297
02:24:12,202 --> 02:24:13,522
[groaning] Let's go.

2298
02:24:14,794 --> 02:24:16,760
What haven't I done for you?

2299
02:24:16,944 --> 02:24:18,555
Have you no gratitude?

2300
02:24:18,594 --> 02:24:19,835
[rod clinks]

2301
02:24:19,859 --> 02:24:22,109
Have you forgotten everything, Jhansi?

2302
02:24:22,187 --> 02:24:24,662
I gave you that name, remember?

2303
02:24:25,206 --> 02:24:26,893
You owe that name...

2304
02:24:26,918 --> 02:24:29,167
and your whole life to me!

2305
02:24:29,200 --> 02:24:31,699
I'm the one who created you.

2306
02:24:32,106 --> 02:24:33,423
-I'm your God.
-[rod whooshes]

2307
02:24:33,448 --> 02:24:34,719
[screams]

2308
02:24:34,744 --> 02:24:36,349
God? Are you serious?

2309
02:24:41,605 --> 02:24:42,980
Are you real right now?

2310
02:24:44,538 --> 02:24:48,371
You found me at a time
I didn't know between right and wrong.

2311
02:24:48,663 --> 02:24:50,205
You brainwashed me into thinking...

2312
02:24:50,246 --> 02:24:52,955
you were God, and what you
said were the ultimate prophecy.

2313
02:24:53,811 --> 02:24:55,311
But people change.

2314
02:24:55,873 --> 02:24:57,664
We eventually uncover the truth.

2315
02:24:57,689 --> 02:24:59,230
You are not God, after all.

2316
02:24:59,877 --> 02:25:02,628
You're a monster that slowly
sucks the life out of someone.

2317
02:25:03,250 --> 02:25:07,083
Jhansi died the day
she realized the truth.

2318
02:25:08,894 --> 02:25:10,436
But I made one mistake though.

2319
02:25:10,745 --> 02:25:11,829
Instead of jail,

2320
02:25:13,058 --> 02:25:14,631
I should've sent you to hell.

2321
02:25:15,245 --> 02:25:16,147
[rod whooshes]

2322
02:25:16,171 --> 02:25:17,187
[gun clicks]

2323
02:25:17,212 --> 02:25:18,296
Go ahead and try!

2324
02:25:19,130 --> 02:25:20,923
I'll take you along with me.

2325
02:25:22,542 --> 02:25:23,359
[rod whooshes]

2326
02:25:23,383 --> 02:25:24,385
[gun shot fired]

2327
02:25:24,409 --> 02:25:25,383
[groans]

2328
02:25:28,576 --> 02:25:30,035
[groans]

2329
02:25:44,392 --> 02:25:46,082
You hit the right spot.

2330
02:25:47,033 --> 02:25:48,378
I won't make it anymore.

2331
02:25:49,700 --> 02:25:50,940
Jhansi...

2332
02:25:52,497 --> 02:25:54,247
You think I'm still scared of dying?

2333
02:25:56,517 --> 02:25:57,753
[coughs]

2334
02:26:01,524 --> 02:26:03,543
[panting] Just look at yourself!

2335
02:26:04,137 --> 02:26:06,407
Let me repeat your math back to you.

2336
02:26:08,309 --> 02:26:09,934
When I die,

2337
02:26:11,098 --> 02:26:12,891
I have people who would mourn for me.

2338
02:26:13,751 --> 02:26:14,958
[groans]

2339
02:26:14,982 --> 02:26:16,565
People who would miss me.

2340
02:26:18,555 --> 02:26:19,681
But when you die,

2341
02:26:19,706 --> 02:26:22,998
people would celebrate
and call it good riddance.

2342
02:26:27,309 --> 02:26:29,274
Shut your eyes for 5 minutes.

2343
02:26:32,766 --> 02:26:34,621
Do some meditation.

2344
02:26:35,848 --> 02:26:37,709
You'll understand what I'm saying.

2345
02:26:39,042 --> 02:26:40,055
Now be gone.

2346
02:26:47,430 --> 02:26:48,662
I'll be gone.

2347
02:26:50,287 --> 02:26:52,473
But only after I watch you die.

2348
02:26:53,796 --> 02:26:55,400
That's when I'll die.

2349
02:26:56,665 --> 02:26:57,801
Let's see about that.

2350
02:26:58,477 --> 02:26:59,469
[gasps]

2351
02:27:00,151 --> 02:27:01,114
Let's...

2352
02:27:01,981 --> 02:27:02,951
Let's see.

2353
02:27:24,564 --> 02:27:25,815
[matchstick strikes]

2354
02:27:28,119 --> 02:27:30,265
Did you get used to your in-laws' routine?

2355
02:27:30,465 --> 02:27:32,507
-They only got used to mine.
-As expected.

2356
02:27:32,898 --> 02:27:33,788
Mother-in-law!

2357
02:27:42,554 --> 02:27:43,721
Sing the prayer, dear.

2358
02:27:43,746 --> 02:27:44,871
Shall I sing?

2359
02:27:45,116 --> 02:27:46,969
-Sure?
-I learned it.

2360
02:27:47,389 --> 02:27:48,422
Go ahead.

2361
02:27:51,812 --> 02:27:53,972
[singing off-key)

2362
02:28:16,249 --> 02:28:18,249
[everyone singing]

2363
02:28:40,700 --> 02:28:41,995
[intense music sets in]

2364
02:28:55,998 --> 02:28:58,398
Who is this guy, walking right in?

2365
02:29:00,238 --> 02:29:01,196
Who are you, sir?

2366
02:29:01,624 --> 02:29:03,077
My wife...

2367
02:29:03,118 --> 02:29:04,766
Stop. Who are you?

2368
02:29:05,410 --> 02:29:07,618
The last guy who showed up
like this gave us a lot of trouble.

2369
02:29:07,643 --> 02:29:10,887
-Who are you here for?
-My wife.

2370
02:29:11,075 --> 02:29:12,783
She said she's going to her
friend and never came back.

2371
02:29:12,897 --> 02:29:15,380
-Oh, you're Kiranmayi's husband?
-Hmm.

2372
02:29:15,405 --> 02:29:17,489
Come, you're family now.

2373
02:29:17,514 --> 02:29:19,931
Come in. You're really
famous in our family.

2374
02:29:20,413 --> 02:29:22,705
Look who it is. Kiranmayi's husband.

2375
02:29:24,520 --> 02:29:26,336
She came here because he was hitting her.

2376
02:29:26,600 --> 02:29:29,945
-You should be ashamed.
-What?

2377
02:29:30,010 --> 02:29:32,927
-You shouldn't have done that.
-What are you saying?

2378
02:29:32,952 --> 02:29:35,577
-I would've sent you to jail.
-Jail?

2379
02:29:37,011 --> 02:29:39,582
-Kiranmayi... Kiranmayi...
-My dear.

2380
02:29:39,607 --> 02:29:41,691
I said I'd come
in 2 days, right?

2381
02:29:41,716 --> 02:29:43,177
Why did you come running?

2382
02:29:43,267 --> 02:29:46,641
I told you my husband
can't stay away for long.

2383
02:29:46,666 --> 02:29:50,801
The last time you said 2
days, you stayed for a week.

2384
02:29:50,826 --> 02:29:53,189
So I didn't make the
mistake of waiting this time.

2385
02:29:53,214 --> 02:29:56,427
My friend insisted that I stay.

2386
02:29:56,452 --> 02:29:57,866
Bless me. You came all the way.

2387
02:29:57,891 --> 02:30:00,933
Look, he's hitting her again.

2388
02:30:01,349 --> 02:30:03,765
I'm not hitting her. I'm saying hi.

2389
02:30:04,474 --> 02:30:05,861
What did you tell them?

2390
02:30:05,886 --> 02:30:08,249
They're trying to send me to jail.

2391
02:30:08,274 --> 02:30:13,087
I told a small lie for
my friend, that's it.

2392
02:30:13,112 --> 02:30:15,316
Friend, friend, friend!

2393
02:30:15,349 --> 02:30:18,473
I want to talk to your friend right now!

2394
02:30:19,341 --> 02:30:20,758
-Are you the friend?
-I'm sorry.

2395
02:30:20,783 --> 02:30:22,034
I only asked her to come.

2396
02:30:22,227 --> 02:30:24,747
Sorry? You think that would suffice?

2397
02:30:24,793 --> 02:30:28,186
I'm doing all the house chores,
wiping my kids' asses. It's painful.

2398
02:30:28,211 --> 02:30:29,211
What kind of friendship is this?

2399
02:30:29,236 --> 02:30:32,487
Behind every best wife, there's a
best husband waiting for her at home.

2400
02:30:33,806 --> 02:30:34,553
What's wrong?

2401
02:30:34,577 --> 02:30:38,974
I've had quite the rough life as a kid.

2402
02:30:38,999 --> 02:30:40,722
Why mention it now?

2403
02:30:41,527 --> 02:30:45,242
I wanted a family and a
home that I could call my own.

2404
02:30:46,543 --> 02:30:48,793
No, no. He didn't mean to ask.

2405
02:30:49,242 --> 02:30:52,159
I bought ribbons and
talcum powder for her...

2406
02:30:52,184 --> 02:30:55,263
with the money I saved at the orphanage.

2407
02:30:55,288 --> 02:30:56,803
You don't have to go
that far back in time.

2408
02:30:56,827 --> 02:30:57,590
Let her speak.

2409
02:30:57,614 --> 02:31:04,566
Then a family adopted
her, leaving me behind.

2410
02:31:04,936 --> 02:31:09,400
Swarna, I'll make him sit
down and tell the whole story.

2411
02:31:09,425 --> 02:31:11,043
-Sure.
-100%.

2412
02:31:11,067 --> 02:31:14,376
-And you will listen?
-Yes, only if she narrates it like you.

2413
02:31:14,658 --> 02:31:15,658
Awesome.

2414
02:31:16,670 --> 02:31:17,618
You should be happy.

2415
02:31:17,643 --> 02:31:20,768
And don't worry. She will
stay right here, and so will I.

2416
02:31:20,793 --> 02:31:23,045
We will stay in a small room, don't worry.

2417
02:31:23,242 --> 02:31:24,095
I'm here for you.

2418
02:31:29,066 --> 02:31:30,566
Don't cry, dear.

2419
02:31:32,119 --> 02:31:33,411
Your friend is gold.

2420
02:31:34,344 --> 02:31:35,297
Bangaram (gold in Telugu)

2421
02:31:35,322 --> 02:31:36,239
Same thing.

